(1520, 'Why is calling \'new ConcreteService()\' inside a domain class an architectural anti-pattern?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nHardcodes the dependency to a concrete implementation, preventing unit testing with mocks and violating DIP.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1863, 'How does std::format in C++20 replace printf and std::stringstream with type-safe high-speed formatting?', '### Advanced Modern C++ Engineering\n\nProvides Python-like formatting syntax ({:02x}), compile-time format string validation, and superior performance compared to iostreams.\n\n#### Core Principle:\nLeverage zero-cost abstractions, RAII resource management, and compile-time type safety.', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
