(1509, 'How does Return Type Covariance in PHP 7.4+ uphold the Liskov Substitution Principle?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nAllows child classes to return more specific subtypes of the parent return type safely.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1510, 'How does Parameter Type Contravariance in PHP 7.4+ comply with LSP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nAllows child methods to accept wider, more generic parameter types than their parent methods.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1511, 'What is Interface Pollution and how to detect it during PHP code reviews?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nLook for empty methods, methods returning dummy booleans, or classes forced to implement irrelevant methods.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1512, 'How does the Decorator Pattern enable OCP for caching and logging in PHP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nWraps existing classes to add caching or logging without editing the underlying service source code.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1513, 'How to test multi-step transactional use cases with mocked DIP interfaces in PHPUnit?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nMock repository and payment interfaces to verify orchestration without hitting physical databases.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1514, 'How do Event Listeners and Domain Events decouple side effects according to SRP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nDomain dispatches OrderCreatedEvent, and independent listeners handle secondary tasks (SMS, Email, Analytics).\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1515, 'What is the Law of Demeter and how does it prevent tight coupling in PHP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nAvoids train-wreck chained calls ($order->getUser()->getWallet()->charge()) by delegating actions to immediate neighbors.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1516, 'How do PHP 8.2 readonly classes enforce immutability and Single Responsibility?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nReadonly classes guarantee all properties are initialized once, making DTOs and Value Objects strictly immutable.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `category`) VALUES
(1517, 'How does the Strategy Pattern implement OCP in PHP shipping rate calculations?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nEncapsulate FedEx, DHL, and UPS shipping algorithms in dedicated strategy classes implementing ShippingCalculatorInterface.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1518, 'What are Class Invariants and Preconditions in Liskov Substitution Principle?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nPreconditions cannot be made stricter in subtypes; postconditions cannot be made weaker; class invariants must remain true.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1519, 'How do PHP SPL interfaces (Countable, Iterator, ArrayAccess) demonstrate ISP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nPHP separates collection capabilities into small, composable role interfaces instead of a giant monolithic Collection class.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1499, 'How do Event Listeners and Domain Events decouple side effects according to SRP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nDomain dispatches OrderCreatedEvent, and independent listeners handle secondary tasks (SMS, Email, Analytics).\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1500, 'What is the Law of Demeter and how does it prevent tight coupling in PHP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nAvoids train-wreck chained calls ($order->getUser()->getWallet()->charge()) by delegating actions to immediate neighbors.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1501, 'How do PHP 8.2 readonly classes enforce immutability and Single Responsibility?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nReadonly classes guarantee all properties are initialized once, making DTOs and Value Objects strictly immutable.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1502, 'How does the Strategy Pattern implement OCP in PHP shipping rate calculations?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nEncapsulate FedEx, DHL, and UPS shipping algorithms in dedicated strategy classes implementing ShippingCalculatorInterface.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1503, 'What are Class Invariants and Preconditions in Liskov Substitution Principle?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nPreconditions cannot be made stricter in subtypes; postconditions cannot be made weaker; class invariants must remain true.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1504, 'How do PHP SPL interfaces (Countable, Iterator, ArrayAccess) demonstrate ISP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nPHP separates collection capabilities into small, composable role interfaces instead of a giant monolithic Collection class.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1505, 'Why is calling \'new ConcreteService()\' inside a domain class an architectural anti-pattern?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nHardcodes the dependency to a concrete implementation, preventing unit testing with mocks and violating DIP.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1506, 'How does Hexagonal Architecture (Ports & Adapters) apply Dependency Inversion in PHP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nDomain defines Ports (interfaces); Infrastructure provides Adapters (PDO, AWS S3, Stripe), keeping domain pure.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1507, 'How do Value Objects (Money, Email, DateRange) enforce SRP in domain models?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nEncapsulate validation and arithmetic for domain values, removing repetitive validation logic from entities.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1508, 'How does CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) align with SRP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nCommands handle business state mutations; Queries handle high-performance reads, separating write and read responsibilities.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1445, 'Why is calling \'new ConcreteService()\' inside a domain class an architectural anti-pattern?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nHardcodes the dependency to a concrete implementation, preventing unit testing with mocks and violating DIP.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
