(1448, 'How does CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation) align with SRP?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nCommands handle business state mutations; Queries handle high-performance reads, separating write and read responsibilities.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
(1449, 'How does Return Type Covariance in PHP 7.4+ uphold the Liskov Substitution Principle?', '### SOLID Architecture & Clean Code\n\nAllows child classes to return more specific subtypes of the parent return type safely.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nMaintain clean boundaries between business domain logic and technical infrastructure.', 'SOLID Design Principles in PHP'),
