(1580, 'What is a Covering Index in MySQL and why does it eliminate bookmark lookups?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nAn index containing all queried columns in SELECT and WHERE, answering queries directly from RAM without touching disk pages.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1581, 'How do Full-Text Indexes (MATCH ... AGAINST) perform in MySQL?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nUses inverted token index for fast natural language and boolean full-text search across large text columns.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1577, 'How do you configure Master-Slave Read/Write database splitting in PHP?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nDirect INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE to Master DB and load-balance SELECT queries across Read Replicas.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1576, 'How do you resolve \'MySQL server has gone away\' (Error 2006) in long-running PHP daemon workers?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nImplement auto-reconnecting PDO wrappers with ping queries (SELECT 1) and retry loops.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1574, 'What are Common Table Expressions (CTEs) and Recursive CTEs in MySQL 8?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nModularize complex queries and traverse hierarchical tree structures like nested comments and categories.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1575, 'How to configure and tune MySQL innodb_buffer_pool_size for production PHP servers?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nAllocate 50-70% of server RAM to innodb_buffer_pool_size to cache data pages and indexes in memory.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1572, 'What is Database Connection Pooling and how does it optimize high-throughput PHP workloads?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nReuses established TCP/TLS database connections across requests to eliminate connection handshake overhead.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1573, 'How do MySQL Window Functions (ROW_NUMBER, RANK, DENSE_RANK) operate in PHP queries?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nCompute rankings, running totals, and moving averages directly inside SQL without PHP array loops.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1571, 'How do you safely execute bulk multi-row batch inserts in PHP PDO?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nChunk datasets into batches of 500-1000 rows inside a single INSERT INTO table (col1, col2) VALUES (...), (...) statement.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1569, 'How do Stored vs Virtual Generated Columns work in MySQL 8?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nVirtual columns are computed on read; Stored columns are saved to disk and can be indexed.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1570, 'How to properly handle UTC timestamps between PHP DateTimeImmutable and MySQL DATETIME?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nStore all timestamps in UTC in MySQL and convert to user local timezones in the presentation layer.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1568, 'How do you detect and prevent MySQL Deadlocks in high-concurrency PHP applications?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nAcquire locks in consistent table/row order, keep transactions brief, and wrap executions in retry loops.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1567, 'What are MySQL Transaction Isolation Levels (READ COMMITTED vs REPEATABLE READ vs SERIALIZABLE)?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nControls dirty reads, non-repeatable reads, and phantom reads. InnoDB defaults to REPEATABLE READ with MVCC.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1565, 'What is a Covering Index in MySQL and why does it eliminate bookmark lookups?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nAn index containing all queried columns in SELECT and WHERE, answering queries directly from RAM without touching disk pages.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1566, 'How do Full-Text Indexes (MATCH ... AGAINST) perform in MySQL?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nUses inverted token index for fast natural language and boolean full-text search across large text columns.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
