(1534, 'How does the Leftmost Prefix Rule dictate composite (multi-column) index utilization in MySQL?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nIndex (A, B, C) can satisfy filters on (A), (A,B), (A,B,C), but cannot satisfy filters on (B,C) alone.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1523, 'How do Prepared Statements prevent SQL Injection at the database wire protocol level?', '### Prepared Statement Mechanics\n\n1. Query syntax tree is parsed and compiled by MySQL in prepare phase.\n2. Parameters are transmitted separately as pure data, never evaluated as executable SQL.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1524, 'How do you execute atomic multi-table database transactions with rollback in PHP PDO?', '### ACID Transactions with PDO\n\n```php\n$pdo->beginTransaction();\ntry {\n    $pdo->prepare(\'UPDATE wallets SET balance = balance - 50 WHERE id = ?\')->execute([$from]);\n    $pdo->prepare(\'UPDATE wallets SET balance = balance + 50 WHERE id = ?\')->execute([$to]);\n    $pdo->commit();\n} catch (Throwable $e) {\n    $pdo->rollBack();\n    throw $e;\n}\n```', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1525, 'How do you process millions of database rows in PHP without memory exhaustion using unbuffered queries and Generators (yield)?', '### Streaming Big Data with Generators\n\n```php\nfunction streamUsers(PDO $pdo): Generator {\n    $pdo->setAttribute(PDO::MYSQL_ATTR_USE_BUFFERED_QUERY, false);\n    $stmt = $pdo->query(\'SELECT * FROM massive_users\');\n    while ($row = $stmt->fetch()) { yield $row; }\n    $pdo->setAttribute(PDO::MYSQL_ATTR_USE_BUFFERED_QUERY, true);\n}\n```', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1526, 'How do you store, query, and index native JSON columns in MySQL 8 with PHP DTOs?', '### MySQL JSON & PHP DTOs\n\nUse virtual generated columns (`GENERATED ALWAYS AS (settings->>\'$.theme\') STORED`) to index JSON properties for sub-millisecond query execution.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1527, 'What is the N+1 query problem in PHP applications and how do you resolve it via eager loading and JOINs?', '### Resolving N+1 Queries\n\nReplace loops of individual queries with SQL `INNER JOIN` (1 query) or batch eager loading `WHERE id IN (...)` (2 queries).', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1528, 'How do you interpret MySQL EXPLAIN output (type, key, rows, Extra) to optimize slow queries in PHP?', '### EXPLAIN Query Analysis\n\nInspect `type` (const > ref > range > ALL), `key` (index used), and `Extra` (`Using filesort` or `Using temporary` indicate bottlenecks).', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1529, 'How do you implement Pessimistic Locking (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) vs Optimistic Locking in PHP?', '### Pessimistic vs Optimistic Locking\n\n- Pessimistic: `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` acquires row locks during transactions.\n- Optimistic: Atomic `UPDATE table SET stock = stock - 1, version = version + 1 WHERE id = :id AND version = :version` without locking.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1530, 'Why does LIMIT 1000000, 20 degrade performance and how does Keyset (Cursor) Pagination fix it?', '### Keyset Pagination\n\n`OFFSET 1000000` scans 1,000,020 rows. Keyset pagination uses `WHERE id < :last_id ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 20`, seeking index trees in O(log N) time.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1531, 'How do you resolve \'MySQL server has gone away\' (Error 2006) in long-running PHP daemon workers?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nImplement auto-reconnecting PDO wrappers with ping queries (SELECT 1) and retry loops.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1532, 'How do you configure Master-Slave Read/Write database splitting in PHP?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nDirect INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE to Master DB and load-balance SELECT queries across Read Replicas.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1533, 'What are the architectural differences between InnoDB and MyISAM storage engines in MySQL?', '### PHP & MySQL Database Architecture\n\nInnoDB supports ACID transactions, row-level locking, foreign keys, and crash recovery; MyISAM uses table-level locks.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways benchmark queries with `EXPLAIN` and use parameterized prepared statements.', 'PHP & MySQL Core to Advanced'),
(1841, 'What is the difference between `std::shared_ptr` and `std::weak_ptr`, and how is the internal Control Block structured?', '### Shared Pointer Control Block & Weak Pointers\n\n`std::make_shared<T>()` allocates the managed object `T` and the **Control Block** in a single contiguous memory block.\n\n```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    Contiguous Allocation                     |\n|  [Managed Object T] | [Strong Ref Count] | [Weak Ref Count]  |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n- **Strong Ref Count**: Tracks active `std::shared_ptr`s. When it reaches 0, the managed object is destroyed.\n- **Weak Ref Count**: Tracks active `std::weak_ptr`s. Prevents cyclic reference memory leaks. Control block memory is freed only when Weak Ref Count reaches 0.', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1838, 'What is Perfect Forwarding and how does `std::forward` preserve value categories with Universal (Forwarding) References?', '### Perfect Forwarding & Reference Collapsing\n\nWhen `T&&` is used in a template deduction context, it represents a **Forwarding Reference** (Universal Reference).\n\n```cpp\n// Reference Collapsing Rules:\n// & + & -> &\n// & + && -> &\n// && + & -> &\n// && + && -> &&\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid wrapper(T&& arg) {\n    // std::forward<T> preserves whether arg was originally an lvalue or rvalue:\n    process(std::forward<T>(arg));\n}\n```', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1840, 'How does `std::unique_ptr` implement zero-overhead exclusive ownership and how do custom deleters affect its sizeof memory footprint?', '### `std::unique_ptr` & Custom Deleters\n\n```cpp\n// 1. Standard unique_ptr: sizeof is identical to raw pointer (8 bytes on 64-bit)\nstd::unique_ptr<Widget> ptr = std::make_unique<Widget>();\n\n// 2. Stateless lambda / function object deleter: sizeof remains 8 bytes (via Empty Base Optimization - EBO)\nauto statelessDeleter = [](Widget* w) { freeWidget(w); };\nstd::unique_ptr<Widget, decltype(statelessDeleter)> w1(allocWidget(), statelessDeleter);\n\n// 3. Function pointer deleter: sizeof doubles to 16 bytes because pointer to deleter must be stored!\nstd::unique_ptr<FILE, int(*)(FILE*)> f(fopen(\"data.txt\", \"r\"), fclose);\n```', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1839, 'Explain the Rule of Zero, Rule of Three, and Rule of Five in modern C++ resource management.', '### Rule of Zero, Three, and Five\n\n- **Rule of Three (C++98)**: If you implement a Destructor, Copy Constructor, or Copy Assignment, you almost certainly need to implement all 3.\n- **Rule of Five (C++11)**: If you implement any of the Three, also implement Move Constructor and Move Assignment.\n- **Rule of Zero (Modern C++)**: Design classes so they manage no raw resources directly; use standard RAII wrappers (`std::unique_ptr`, `std::vector`, `std::string`) so compiler-generated default special member functions work correctly.', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1837, 'How do Move Semantics work internally and what happens to the source object after `std::move`?', '### Move Semantics Mechanics\n\n`std::move` does not move anything at runtime; it performs an unconditional `static_cast<T&&>(var)` to an rvalue reference, enabling the move constructor or move assignment operator.\n\n```cpp\nclass Buffer {\n    char* data_;\n    size_t size_;\npublic:\n    // Move constructor: transfers ownership with zero allocations\n    Buffer(Buffer&& other) noexcept \n        : data_(other.data_), size_(other.size_) {\n        other.data_ = nullptr; // Leaves source in a valid but unspecified state\n        other.size_ = 0;\n    }\n};\n```', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1836, 'What is the exact distinction between lvalues, rvalues, prvalues, and xvalues (value categories) in modern C++?', '### Modern C++ Value Categories\n\n```\n                    Expressions\n                   /           \\\n              glvalue         rvalue\n             /       \\       /      \\\n          lvalue       xvalue      prvalue\n```\n\n- **lvalue**: Has an identity and cannot be moved from automatically (e.g. named variables `x`, `ptr`).\n- **prvalue (pure rvalue)**: Computes a value without an identity; can initialize objects (e.g. `42`, `x + y`, temporary returned by value).\n- **xvalue (eXpiring value)**: Has an identity and **can** be moved from (e.g. `std::move(x)`, `static_cast<T&&>(x)`).\n- **glvalue**: Has identity (lvalue or xvalue).\n- **rvalue**: Can be moved from (prvalue or xvalue).', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1835, 'How does firstOrFail() vs firstOr() vs sole() operate in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nfirstOrFail throws 404/ModelNotFoundException; firstOr executes closure fallback; sole guarantees exactly 1 record matches or throws exception.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1834, 'How do you define and use Local Scopes with optional parameters in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\npublic function scopeOfType(Builder $query, string $type = \'standard\'): void { $query->where(\'type\', $type); }\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1833, 'How does $touches cascade parent updated_at timestamp updates across child models?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nSetting protected $touches = [\'post\']; on Comment updates the parent post timestamp whenever comment is updated or deleted.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1832, 'How to perform atomic column increments and decrements in Laravel with extra updates?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUser::where(\'id\', $id)->increment(\'credits\', 50, [\'last_awarded_at\' => now()]);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1831, 'How does Schema::dump() and schema squashing accelerate database test suites in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nDumps full SQL schema into a single schema file, bypassing sequential migrations execution in test environments.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1830, 'How to switch database connections per tenant in multi-tenant Laravel systems?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nSet connection at runtime: $model->setConnection(\'tenant_2\'); or DB::purge(\'tenant\'); Config::set(\'database.connections.tenant.database\', $dbName);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1828, 'How to configure and read from Read/Write MySQL connection pools in config/database.php?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nConfigure \'read\' => [\'host\' => [\'10.0.0.1\', \'10.0.0.2\']] and \'write\' => [\'host\' => \'10.0.0.3\'] under mysql driver.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1829, 'How do you force Eloquent to read from the Write (Master) connection for fresh queries?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse Model::onWriteConnection()->find($id); or DB::connection()->useWriteConnection();\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1827, 'How does tap() and when() conditional clauses clean up complex dynamic query builder chains?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\n->when($request->status, fn($q, $s) => $q->where(\'status\', $s))->when($request->search, fn($q, term) => $q->where(\'title\', \'like\', \"%$term%\")).\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1826, 'How do you perform Subquery Ordering in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse ->orderByDesc(Order::select(\'created_at\')->whereColumn(\'user_id\', \'users.id\')->latest()->limit(1)).\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1825, 'How do you perform Subquery Selects using addSelect() in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse $query->addSelect([\'last_login\' => Login::select(\'created_at\')->whereColumn(\'user_id\', \'users.id\')->latest()->limit(1)]);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1823, 'How do you store and query spatial geographic coordinates in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse $table->geometry(\'location\') and query with whereRaw(\'ST_Distance_Sphere(location, POINT(?, ?)) < ?\').\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1824, 'How does whereRaw() and selectRaw() safely bind parameters to prevent SQL injection in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nPass parameter array as 2nd argument: ->whereRaw(\'price > ? AND status = ?\', [100, \'active\']).\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1822, 'How to create composite unique indexes and composite primary keys in Laravel migrations?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse $table->unique([\'user_id\', \'role_id\']); or $table->primary([\'order_id\', \'product_id\']);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1821, 'How do you configure foreignId constraints with cascade on delete in migrations?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse $table->foreignId(\'user_id\')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete()->cascadeOnUpdate();\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1820, 'How to seed massive datasets using Model::insert() vs Model::create() in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nModel::insert($array) executes a single multi-row SQL INSERT, while Model::create() executes individual queries per record with event overhead.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1818, 'How do you map custom date and datetime formats using $casts in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\n\'created_at\' => \'datetime:Y-m-d H:i:s\', \'published_date\' => \'immutable_date:Y-m-d\'.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1819, 'How does DB::listen() help profile slow database queries and memory usage in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nDB::listen(function($query) { if ($query->time > 100) Log::warning(\"Slow query: {$query->sql}\", $query->bindings); });\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1816, 'How to handle Soft Delete unique constraint conflicts in MySQL with Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse composite unique index with deleted_at or MySQL 8 generated columns.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `category`) VALUES
(1817, 'How to configure full-text search indexes in Laravel migrations and query with whereFullText?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\n$table->fullText([\'title\', \'body\']); and Post::whereFullText([\'title\', \'body\'], \'database indexing\')->get();\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1815, 'How does firstOrFail() vs firstOr() vs sole() operate in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nfirstOrFail throws 404/ModelNotFoundException; firstOr executes closure fallback; sole guarantees exactly 1 record matches or throws exception.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1814, 'How do you define and use Local Scopes with optional parameters in Eloquent?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\npublic function scopeOfType(Builder $query, string $type = \'standard\'): void { $query->where(\'type\', $type); }\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1813, 'How does $touches cascade parent updated_at timestamp updates across child models?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nSetting protected $touches = [\'post\']; on Comment updates the parent post timestamp whenever comment is updated or deleted.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1807, 'How does tap() and when() conditional clauses clean up complex dynamic query builder chains?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\n->when($request->status, fn($q, $s) => $q->where(\'status\', $s))->when($request->search, fn($q, term) => $q->where(\'title\', \'like\', \"%$term%\")).\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1808, 'How to configure and read from Read/Write MySQL connection pools in config/database.php?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nConfigure \'read\' => [\'host\' => [\'10.0.0.1\', \'10.0.0.2\']] and \'write\' => [\'host\' => \'10.0.0.3\'] under mysql driver.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1809, 'How do you force Eloquent to read from the Write (Master) connection for fresh queries?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUse Model::onWriteConnection()->find($id); or DB::connection()->useWriteConnection();\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1810, 'How to switch database connections per tenant in multi-tenant Laravel systems?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nSet connection at runtime: $model->setConnection(\'tenant_2\'); or DB::purge(\'tenant\'); Config::set(\'database.connections.tenant.database\', $dbName);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1811, 'How does Schema::dump() and schema squashing accelerate database test suites in Laravel?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nDumps full SQL schema into a single schema file, bypassing sequential migrations execution in test environments.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1812, 'How to perform atomic column increments and decrements in Laravel with extra updates?', '### Laravel Database & Eloquent Engineering\n\nUser::where(\'id\', $id)->increment(\'credits\', 50, [\'last_awarded_at\' => now()]);\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAlways verify query efficiency with `DB::listen()` and enforce strict model modes during development.', 'Laravel Database & Eloquent Mastery'),
(1730, 'What is a Covering Index and how does it prevent disk I/O bookmark lookups?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nAn index containing all SELECT and WHERE columns, answering queries directly from the index tree.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1842, 'What is SFINAE (Substitution Failure Is Not An Error) and how was it used before C++20 Concepts?', '### SFINAE & `std::enable_if`\n\nIf substituting a template type creates an invalid signature, the compiler discards the overload rather than throwing a compile error.\n\n```cpp\ntemplate <typename T>\ntypename std::enable_if<std::is_integral<T>::value, bool>::type\nisEven(T val) {\n    return val % 2 == 0;\n}\n```', 'Advanced Modern C++'),
(1729, 'How do LAG() and LEAD() calculate period-over-period differences in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nAccess preceding and succeeding rows within a partition without self-joins.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1728, 'How do Semi-Joins (EXISTS) and Anti-Joins (NOT EXISTS) operate in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nSemi-join checks existence of matches; Anti-join filters for absence of matches.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1724, 'How do Stored Procedures differ from User-Defined Functions (UDF) in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nProcedures execute transactions and return result sets; Functions return scalar values and can be used inside SELECT.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1725, 'How do Database Triggers work and why should business logic in triggers be limited?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nAutomate actions on DML events; complex triggers obscure business rules and hinder debugging.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1726, 'What is a Correlated Subquery and why is an INNER JOIN often faster?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nCorrelated subqueries execute once per outer row; JOINs allow database optimizers to use hash or merge join algorithms.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1727, 'What is the difference between UNION and UNION ALL in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nUNION performs deduplication sort; UNION ALL concatenates directly without sorting, making it faster.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1722, 'What is the difference between Views and Materialized Views in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nViews execute dynamically on read; Materialized Views persist query results on disk and refresh periodically.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1723, 'How does Table Partitioning (Range, List, Hash) differ from Database Sharding?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nPartitioning divides tables across disks in one instance; Sharding distributes data across multiple independent servers.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1718, 'What are Gap Locks and Next-Key Locks in InnoDB?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nGap locks lock index ranges between records to prevent phantom inserts; Next-Key locks combine record and gap locks.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1719, 'What is Keyset Pagination and why is it superior to OFFSET/LIMIT?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nUses indexed WHERE id < last_id ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 20 for O(log N) index seeks on large datasets.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1720, 'What are the trade-offs between Auto-Increment integers and UUID v7 for Primary Keys?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nAuto-increment causes sequential clustering; UUID v7 provides time-ordered global uniqueness without B-Tree page splits.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1721, 'How do Check Constraints (CHECK) enforce data integrity at the database layer?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nEnsures columns satisfy business rules (e.g. price > 0, age >= 18) before commits.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1717, 'What is MVCC (Multi-Version Concurrency Control) in relational databases?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nMaintains row version snapshots in undo logs so readers don\'t block writers and writers don\'t block readers.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1716, 'What are the 4 ANSI Transaction Isolation Levels and what anomalies do they prevent?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nRead Uncommitted, Read Committed, Repeatable Read, Serializable prevent dirty reads, non-repeatable reads, and phantom reads.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
(1713, 'How do Semi-Joins (EXISTS) and Anti-Joins (NOT EXISTS) operate in SQL?', '### SQL Query Engineering\n\nSemi-join checks existence of matches; Anti-join filters for absence of matches.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAnalyze queries using `EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE` and ensure proper index coverage.', 'SQL Query Mastery & Database Design'),
