(1993, 'What is the difference between Synchronous, Semi-Synchronous, and Asynchronous Database Replication?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nAsync returns immediately after primary commit; Semi-sync waits for at least 1 replica ack; Sync waits for all replicas.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1994, 'How do Covering Indexes achieve Index-Only Scans with zero heap/table access?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nAll columns in SELECT, JOIN, and WHERE exist within the index leaf nodes, answering queries directly from index buffers.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1995, 'What causes Deadlocks in distributed SQL environments and how does a Wait-For Graph resolve them?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nTransactions form circular lock dependencies; the database detects cycles in the Wait-For Graph and terminates the lowest-cost transaction.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1996, 'What are the differences between RANGE BETWEEN and ROWS BETWEEN in window frame specifications?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nROWS counts physical rows; RANGE calculates logical value offsets based on the ORDER BY value.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1997, 'How does the Multi-Version Concurrency Control (MVCC) visibility map and VACUUM operate in PostgreSQL?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nMaintains dead tuples from updates/deletes; VACUUM reclaims storage and updates the visibility map to enable Index-Only Scans.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1998, 'What is an Index Skip Scan and how does the optimizer execute queries without leading index columns?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nSkips through distinct values of the low-cardinality leading column to utilize the secondary indexed column efficiently.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(1999, 'What is the difference between Optimistic Concurrency Control and Two-Phase Locking (2PL)?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nOCC validates on commit without locking; 2PL acquires growing locks in phase 1 and releases shrinking locks in phase 2.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2000, 'How does Bitmap Index Scan combine multiple secondary indexes in an execution plan?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nConverts matching rows from multiple indexes into in-memory bitmaps and performs bitwise AND/OR operations before reading data pages.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2001, 'How do Partial (Filtered) Indexes minimize storage and increase cache hit ratios?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nIndexes only rows satisfying a predicate (e.g. WHERE status = \'unprocessed\'), saving RAM and write overhead.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2002, 'How does Two-Phase Commit (2PC) maintain atomic transactions across distributed database shards?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nCoordinator sends Prepare phase to all participants; if all vote yes, sends Commit phase; otherwise sends Abort.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2003, 'What are the mechanics of Lock Escalation and how to prevent table-level locking in high-throughput workloads?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nDatabase converts thousands of fine-grained row locks into a single table lock when memory thresholds are exceeded.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2004, 'How do Common Table Expressions (CTEs) behave when declared MATERIALIZED vs NOT MATERIALIZED?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nMATERIALIZED evaluates the CTE once as an internal temporary table; NOT MATERIALIZED inlines the CTE into the main query plan.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2005, 'What are Adaptive Hash Indexes in MySQL InnoDB and how do they speed up B+Tree lookups?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nInnoDB automatically builds in-memory hash indexes on frequently accessed B+Tree leaf pages for O(1) buffer lookups.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
(2006, 'How do You pivot dynamic rows to columns using conditional aggregation in SQL?', '### Advanced SQL & Database Internals\n\nUse SELECT category, SUM(CASE WHEN month = 1 THEN sales ELSE 0 END) AS jan_sales GROUP BY category.\n\n#### Engineering Guideline:\nAnalyze query execution plans with `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` and design indexes matching the underlying storage engine.', 'Advanced SQL & Database Internals'),
