(2111, 'How does standalone Docker deployment (output: \'standalone\') optimize Next.js production builds?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nTraces node_modules and bundles only the necessary files into .next/standalone, reducing Docker image size by over 80%.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2112, 'What are the trade-offs between Edge Runtime and Node.js Runtime in Route Handlers?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nEdge runtime provides global low latency and instant cold starts with limited Node APIs; Node.js runtime provides full Node.js API support.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2113, 'How do catch-all ([...slug]) and optional catch-all ([[...slug]]) dynamic routes differ?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nCatch-all requires at least 1 segment (/docs/a); Optional catch-all also matches the root route (/docs) without parameters.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2114, 'How to handle global errors using global-error.tsx and not-found.tsx in Next.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nglobal-error.tsx catches errors in root layout; not-found.tsx renders custom 404 UI when notFound() is triggered.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2115, 'How does Turbopack accelerate local development and hot module reloading in Next.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nRust-based incremental bundler that caches function-level compilation results for sub-50ms HMR updates.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2116, 'What is the difference between layouts.tsx and templates.tsx in Next.js App Router?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nLayouts preserve state and do not re-render on navigation between sibling routes; Templates create a new instance and reset state/effects on every navigation.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2117, 'How does Route Group syntax (group) organize folders without affecting the URL structure?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nWrapping folder names in parentheses e.g. (marketing) or (dashboard) groups routes logically without adding /marketing to the URL path.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2118, 'How do you prevent sensitive backend code leaks using the server-only package in Next.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nImporting \'server-only\' in a utility or database file throws a build-time compile error if accidentally imported into a Client Component.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2119, 'How do revalidatePath() and revalidateTag() purge Next.js Data Cache on-demand?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nrevalidateTag(\'products\') invalidates all cached fetch requests tagged with \'products\'; revalidatePath(\'/blog\') revalidates specific route path caches.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2120, 'What are the differences between dynamicParams true and false in dynamic App Router segments?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nWhen dynamicParams is false, visiting a dynamic route not generated by generateStaticParams returns a 404 instead of rendering on-demand.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2121, 'How does the useOptimistic hook provide instant UI feedback during Server Action execution?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nDisplays optimistic state updates immediately while awaiting server response; automatically rolls back if the server action throws an error.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2122, 'How do useFormStatus and useActionState (useFormState) manage form pending states in Next.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nuseFormStatus exposes pending boolean to submit buttons; useActionState manages action return state and error messages.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2123, 'How to configure custom HTTP headers, CSP, and CORS in Next.js next.config.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nDefine async headers() returning source pattern and key-value arrays for Content-Security-Policy and CORS headers.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2124, 'What is the difference between unstable_cache and standard fetch caching in Next.js?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nunstable_cache wraps arbitrary async database or ORM functions (e.g. Prisma queries) with Next.js Data Cache and tag revalidation.\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
(2125, 'How do you implement internationalization (i18n) routing with App Router middleware?', '### Next.js App Router Architecture\n\nUse middleware to detect user Accept-Language headers and rewrite paths to localized route groups (e.g. /[lang]/about).\n\n#### Best Practice:\nAdopt a Server-First mental model: keep components as Server Components by default, and push `\'use client\'` down to the interactive leaf nodes of your component tree.', 'Next.js App Router & Full-Stack Architecture'),
