(2227, 'What are Geospatial 2dsphere indexes and how do $nearSphere and $geoWithin query coordinates?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nIndexes Earth spherical geometry (GeoJSON Point, Polygon) to calculate distances and radius queries in meters.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2228, 'How does the WiredTiger Storage Engine allocate memory for its internal cache vs OS filesystem cache?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nAllocates 50% of (RAM - 1GB) to WiredTiger cache for uncompressed pages; remaining RAM used by OS filesystem cache for compressed disk I/O.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2229, 'What is an Arbiter in MongoDB Replica Sets and why is a dedicated data-bearing secondary preferred in modern architecture?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nAn arbiter participates in voting during elections without holding data; can cause split-brain edge cases if network partitions occur.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2230, 'How does the Outlier Pattern handle skewed data distributions (e.g. a celebrity with 10 million followers)?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nStores standard users with embedded arrays and flags outliers with hasOverflow: true, storing overflow followers in a separate collection.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2231, 'What is the difference between $set, $unset, $inc, and $mul update operators in MongoDB?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\n$set updates fields, $unset removes fields, $inc increments numeric counters atomically, $mul multiplies values.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2232, 'How does Read Preference (primaryPreferred, secondaryPreferred, nearest) affect query routing and replication lag?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nDirects reads to secondaries for reporting but exposes application to stale data due to asynchronous replication lag.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2233, 'What is a Targeted Query vs a Broadcast (Scatter-Gather) Query in a sharded MongoDB cluster?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nTargeted queries include the Shard Key in WHERE clause (routed to 1 shard); Broadcast queries lack Shard Key and query all shards.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2234, 'How does Text Indexing with $text and $meta textScore calculate search relevance rankings in MongoDB?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nCreates an inverted stem token index and scores documents based on keyword frequency and weight multipliers.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2235, 'How does the Subset Pattern improve performance for pages that only display recent reviews or top comments?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nEmbeds the 5 most recent reviews in the main product document and loads remaining historical reviews on demand from a secondary collection.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2236, 'How do TTL (Time-To-Live) Indexes automatically expire and delete ephemeral documents in MongoDB?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\ndb.sessions.createIndex({ createdAt: 1 }, { expireAfterSeconds: 3600 }) automatically removes documents after 1 hour via background thread.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2237, 'What are Partial Indexes and how do they save RAM and disk compared to Sparse Indexes?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nPartial indexes use a filter expression (e.g. { partialFilterExpression: { rating: { $gt: 4 } } }) to index only relevant subset of documents.\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced'),
(2238, 'How do Multi-Document ACID Transactions operate with client sessions in MongoDB 4.0+?', '### MongoDB Document Database Engineering\n\nUses session.startTransaction(), performs CRUD across collections, and commits atomically with session.commitTransaction().\n\n#### Core Architectural Principle:\nDesign schemas based on your application\'s data access patterns, and always verify index coverage with `explain(\'executionStats\')`.', 'MongoDB Document Database from Zero to Advanced');
