(2404, 'How do Redis Streams (XADD, XREADGROUP) differ from standard Redis Pub/Sub in event-driven microservices?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nPub/sub is fire-and-forget (lost if subscriber offline); Streams persist event logs on disk and support Consumer Groups and message acknowledgments (XACK).\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2405, 'How to configure multi-tenant cache separation using dynamic Redis key prefixes in Laravel?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nSet \'prefix\' => \'tenant_\' . tenant(\'id\') . \':\' in config/database.php or use Redis::connection(\'tenant\')->setPrefix().\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2406, 'How does Redis HyperLogLog (PFADD, PFCOUNT) count 100 million unique IP addresses with only 12KB RAM?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nUses probabilistic cardinality estimation with fixed 12KB memory and a standard error rate of 0.81%.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2407, 'How to handle Redis connection timeouts, retries, and read/write timeouts in config/database.php?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nConfigure \'read_timeout\' => 2.5, \'timeout\' => 2.0, and \'retry_interval\' => 100 in the Redis connection options.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2408, 'How does the Redlock algorithm implement fault-tolerant distributed locking across multi-node Redis clusters?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nAcquires locks across N independent master nodes (quorum of N/2 + 1) within a strict time limit to prevent split-brain locks.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2409, 'How to use Redis Bitmaps (SETBIT, GETBIT, BITCOUNT) to track daily active user retention in Laravel?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nStores 1 bit per user ID (1 = active, 0 = inactive); 1 million daily active users consume only ~122KB RAM.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2410, 'What is the difference between Redis pipeline() and transaction() (MULTI/EXEC) in Laravel?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\npipeline() sends batch commands asynchronously to reduce network round-trips; transaction() ensures atomic isolated execution with MULTI/EXEC.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2411, 'How do you configure Redis Geospatial indexes (GEOADD, GEODIST, GEORADIUS) in Laravel?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nStores longitude/latitude in Sorted Sets using 52-bit geohashes for fast radius and proximity calculations.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `category`) VALUES
(2412, 'How to prevent Redis memory fragmentation and optimize the memory allocator (Jemalloc)?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nMonitor memory fragmentation ratio (used_memory_rss / used_memory); trigger active defragmentation with activedefrag yes in redis.conf.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2413, 'How does the XFetch (Probabilistic Early Expiration) algorithm prevent cache stampedes without explicit locks?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nRecomputes and refreshes cached items probabilistically before the actual TTL expires, smoothing out database load.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2414, 'How do you configure Redis as a high-performance session handler in Laravel (SESSION_DRIVER=redis)?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nStores serialized user session payloads in Redis with automated TTL expiration, decoupling session storage from web servers.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2415, 'How to safely flush or clear specific tagged keys in Redis without calling FLUSHDB in production?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nNever call FLUSHDB in production; use SCAN with MATCH pattern and UNLINK (asynchronous non-blocking deletion).\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2416, 'How do Cache Tags (Cache::tags([\'users\', \'reports\'])) work internally in Redis and what is the invalidation overhead?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nLaravel creates tag namespaces in Redis using UUIDs; invalidating a tag increments the tag version key, instantly making all child cached keys unreachable.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2417, 'What are the differences between RDB (Snapshotting) and AOF (Append-Only File) persistence in Redis?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nRDB takes periodic point-in-time binary dumps (fast recovery, small disk); AOF logs every write command (zero data loss, larger files).\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2418, 'How does Redis Pub/Sub integrate with Laravel Event Broadcasting and Laravel Reverb / WebSockets?', '### Redis & Laravel Architecture\n\nBroadcast events publish to Redis channels; WebSockets servers (Reverb/Soketi) subscribe to channels and push messages to frontend browsers.\n\n#### Architectural Rule:\nIsolate Cache and Queue Redis instances, enforce connection timeouts, and use atomic distributed locks to prevent race conditions.', 'Redis & Laravel Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
