(2507, 'How does SSL/TLS (WSS) integration with OpenSSL operate in C++ WebSocket servers?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nWraps standard TCP stream in an SSL_CTX / SSL socket, performing TLS 1.3 handshake and encrypting frame bytes before socket transmission.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2508, 'What is the difference between Text Frames (0x1) and Binary Frames (0x2) in WebSocket protocols?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nText frames must be strictly validated as valid UTF-8 sequences (invalid UTF-8 triggers 1007 Close); Binary frames contain raw unvalidated bytes.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2509, 'How do Continuation Frames (0x0) handle large streamed messages across multiple WebSocket chunks?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nFirst frame has FIN=0 and opcode (text/binary); intermediate frames have FIN=0 and opcode 0x0; final frame has FIN=1 and opcode 0x0.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2510, 'How does lock-free single-producer single-consumer (SPSC) ring buffer architecture optimize multi-threaded WebSocket broadcasting?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nEnables worker threads to push outbound messages to network threads with zero mutex contention and sub-50 nanosecond latency.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2511, 'How to configure TCP_NODELAY and SO_REUSEPORT on C++ WebSocket listening sockets?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nTCP_NODELAY disables Nagle algorithm for instant packet dispatch; SO_REUSEPORT allows multiple processes to bind same port for kernel load balancing.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2512, 'How does WebSocket++ handle connection management via trait-based configuration in C++?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nAllows customizing TLS, Asio, and logging backends at compile time via template policy traits without runtime overhead.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2513, 'What is the difference between Reactor and Proactor network architectural patterns in C++ servers?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nReactor notifies when a socket is ready to read/write (epoll); Proactor initiates async I/O and notifies when transfer completes (IOCP, io_uring).\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2514, 'How do you build a multi-node WebSocket cluster with Redis Pub/Sub backplane in C++?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nEach C++ server subscribes to Redis channels; when a node receives a broadcast, it fans out to its local connected WebSockets.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2515, 'How to detect and mitigate Slowloris and Frame Flooding attacks against C++ WebSocket servers?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nEnforce strict handshake timeout limits, minimum byte transfer rates, and cap max uncompressed frame size (e.g. 64KB).\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2516, 'How does ALPN (Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation) negotiate HTTP/1.1 vs HTTP/2 before WebSocket upgrade?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nAllows TLS handshake to select protocol version before sending cleartext HTTP upgrade headers.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2517, 'What are the memory layout benefits of using Simple Binary Encoding (SBE) for WebSocket streaming in FinTech?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nSBE uses fixed-offset binary structs, enabling direct struct pointer casting on received WebSocket buffers with zero parsing latency.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2518, 'How to profile WebSocket memory allocation bottlenecks and latency jitter with perf and Valgrind Massif?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nIdentify hot allocation paths in onMessage callbacks and replace dynamic std::string allocations with memory arena pools.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2519, 'How does Thread-per-Core architecture eliminate inter-thread lock contention in modern C++ network servers?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nAssigns 1 event loop per CPU core; each connection is owned by a single thread for its entire lifecycle, eliminating locking.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2520, 'How do you implement client-side automatic reconnection with exponential backoff and jitter in C++ WebSocket clients?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nCalculates backoff delay = min(max_delay, base * 2^attempt) + random_jitter to prevent thundering herd reconnections to servers.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
(2521, 'What are WebSocket Close Codes (1000 Normal, 1001 Going Away, 1006 Abnormal, 1008 Policy Violation)?', '### High-Performance C++ WebSockets\n\nStandard status codes sent inside Close frames to explain disconnection reasons according to RFC 6455.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Rule:\nDisable Nagle\'s algorithm (`TCP_NODELAY`), implement backpressure high-watermark checks, and use zero-copy binary serialization formats (FlatBuffers/SBE).', 'High-Performance WebSockets in C++'),
