(2611, 'How does TCP Small Queues (TSQ) and BQL (Byte Queue Limits) eliminate bufferbloat in high-throughput C++ WebSocket servers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nLimits amount of unacknowledged data buffered inside kernel queues, keeping socket RTT and delivery jitter minimal.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2612, 'What are the architectural trade-offs of Kernel-Bypass networking (Solarflare OpenOnload / DPDK) for C++ WebSockets?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nBypasses Linux TCP/IP stack to read packets directly from NIC memory, reducing latency to <500ns at the cost of dedicated CPU polling.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2613, 'How does TLS 1.3 0-RTT Early Data work over WebSockets and how do you protect against Replay Attacks?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nClient sends encrypted data in initial TLS handshake packet; server rejects non-idempotent early requests to prevent replay attacks.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2614, 'What are the memory layout benefits of Structure of Arrays (SoA) vs Array of Structures (AoS) in WebSocket connection state managers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nSoA groups same-attribute arrays contiguously in RAM, maximizing CPU cache line efficiency during broadcast loops.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2615, 'How do you manage sequence numbers and gap detection for L3 Full Order Book delta replication over WebSockets?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nAttach monotonically increasing sequence ID to every frame; client requests snapshot resync if missing sequence numbers are detected.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2616, 'How does memory fence ordering (acquire/release vs sequential consistency) impact atomic session publication in multithreaded servers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nAcquire-release enforces memory visibility boundaries across cores without issuing expensive full bus-lock instructions (MFENCE).\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2617, 'What is Zero-Copy TCP streaming with vmsplice() and tee() syscalls in Linux C++ servers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nMoves memory pages directly between user memory and pipe buffers without copying data bytes through the CPU.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2618, 'How do you configure SO_INCOMING_CPU to route WebSocket socket events to the CPU core handling NIC interrupts?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nAligns kernel softirq processing with user-space worker thread to achieve perfect CPU cache warmth for TCP packets.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2619, 'How does fastutf8 validation achieve 4GB/sec validation throughput for incoming WebSocket text frames?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nUses SIMD lookup tables to validate UTF-8 byte sequences in parallel chunks rather than state machine branches.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2620, 'What is the difference between Aeron IPC shared memory transport and WebSockets for local intra-host messaging?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nAeron IPC uses memory-mapped files and lock-free rings for sub-100ns IPC; WebSockets bridge external network clients.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2621, 'How to design a resilient distributed WebSocket fan-out cluster using NATS JetStream and Kafka backplanes in C++?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nWorker nodes consume partitioned Kafka streams and fan out binary frames to millions of connected WebSocket clients.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2622, 'How to detect memory leaks and trace allocator performance under 1M concurrent WebSocket connections using Jemalloc profiling?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nEnable MALLOC_CONF=prof:true to generate heap allocation dumps and identify memory fragmentation hot-spots.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2623, 'What are the mechanics of RFC 6455 RSV bits (RSV1, RSV2, RSV3) for custom protocol extensions in C++?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nRSV bits signal custom frame compression, end-to-end encryption, or proprietary multiplexing layers.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2624, 'How does epoll edge-triggered (EPOLLET) mode differ from level-triggered mode when draining large WebSocket frame queues?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nEdge-triggered notifies only on state transitions; workers must loop read()/write() until EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK is returned.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2625, 'How to benchmark and measure tail latency (p99, p99.9, p99.99) jitter in C++ WebSocket servers under synthetic load?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nUse HDRHistogram to measure high-percentile latency distributions without falling victim to the Coordinated Omission problem.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
