(2671, 'How does TCP Small Queues (TSQ) and BQL (Byte Queue Limits) eliminate bufferbloat in high-throughput C++ WebSocket servers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nLimits amount of unacknowledged data buffered inside kernel queues, keeping socket RTT and delivery jitter minimal.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2672, 'What are the architectural trade-offs of Kernel-Bypass networking (Solarflare OpenOnload / DPDK) for C++ WebSockets?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nBypasses Linux TCP/IP stack to read packets directly from NIC memory, reducing latency to <500ns at the cost of dedicated CPU polling.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2673, 'How does TLS 1.3 0-RTT Early Data work over WebSockets and how do you protect against Replay Attacks?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nClient sends encrypted data in initial TLS handshake packet; server rejects non-idempotent early requests to prevent replay attacks.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2674, 'What are the memory layout benefits of Structure of Arrays (SoA) vs Array of Structures (AoS) in WebSocket connection state managers?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nSoA groups same-attribute arrays contiguously in RAM, maximizing CPU cache line efficiency during broadcast loops.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2675, 'How do you manage sequence numbers and gap detection for L3 Full Order Book delta replication over WebSockets?', '### Advanced C++ WebSocket & Low-Latency Architecture\n\nAttach monotonically increasing sequence ID to every frame; client requests snapshot resync if missing sequence numbers are detected.\n\n#### Low-Latency Engineering Standard:\nUtilize `io_uring` with SQPOLL, pin threads to isolated NUMA cores, and enforce SIMD vectorization for frame parsing.', 'Advanced C++ WebSocket Internals & Low-Latency Systems'),
(2676, 'Why is standard PHP-FPM / Apache unable to handle WebSockets, and how do CLI event loops solve persistent connections?', '### PHP-FPM Limitations & CLI Event Loops\n\n- **PHP-FPM (Request-Response)**: Spawns one process/thread per HTTP request, immediately terminating when the response finishes (`die()` / `exit()`). Holding 10,000 idle WebSocket connections on PHP-FPM would spawn 10,000 OS processes, instantly exhausting server RAM and crashing the server.\n- **CLI Event Loops (ReactPHP / Swoole / Workerman)**: A single persistent PHP CLI process listens on a non-blocking TCP socket using an event loop (`epoll`/`kqueue`), multiplexing thousands of concurrent persistent connections within a single thread with minimal RAM usage.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2677, 'How do you build a pure WebSocket server in PHP using Ratchet (`cboden/ratchet`) and ReactPHP?', '### Ratchet WebSocket Server in PHP\n\n```php\nuse Ratchet\\MessageComponentInterface;\nuse Ratchet\\ConnectionInterface;\nuse Ratchet\\Server\\IoServer;\nuse Ratchet\\Http\\HttpServer;\nuse Ratchet\\WebSocket\\WsServer;\n\nrequire __DIR__ . \'/vendor/autoload.php\';\n\nclass ChatServer implements MessageComponentInterface {\n    protected SplObjectStorage $clients;\n\n    public function __construct() {\n        $this->clients = new SplObjectStorage();\n    }\n\n    public function onOpen(ConnectionInterface $conn): void {\n        $this->clients->attach($conn);\n        echo \"New connection! ({$conn->resourceId})\\n\";\n    }\n\n    public function onMessage(ConnectionInterface $from, $msg): void {\n        // Broadcast message to all connected clients:\n        foreach ($this->clients as $client) {\n            if ($from !== $client) {\n                $client->send($msg);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    public function onClose(ConnectionInterface $conn): void {\n        $this->clients->detach($conn);\n        echo \"Connection {$conn->resourceId} has disconnected\\n\";\n    }\n\n    public function onError(ConnectionInterface $conn, \\Exception $e): void {\n        $conn->close();\n    }\n}\n\n$server = IoServer::factory(\n    new HttpServer(new WsServer(new ChatServer())),\n    8080\n);\n$server->run();\n```', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `category`) VALUES
(2678, 'How does Swoole (`ext-swoole`) achieve 100K+ concurrent WebSocket connections in PHP using coroutines and multi-process workers?', '### Swoole WebSocket Server Architecture\n\nSwoole is a compiled C/C++ PHP extension providing asynchronous coroutines and high-performance network servers.\n\n```\n[Incoming Connections] ---> [Master Thread (epoll)] ---> [Manager Process]\n                                                                 |\n                                                 +---------------+---------------+\n                                                 | (Task/Worker) | (Task/Worker) |\n                                             [Worker 1]      [Worker 2]      [Worker N]\n```\n\n```php\n$server = new Swoole\\WebSocket\\Server(\'0.0.0.0\', 9501);\n\n$server->set([\n    \'worker_num\' => 4,         // Number of worker processes\n    \'max_connection\' => 100000, // Maximum concurrent connections\n    \'enable_coroutine\' => true, // Enable async coroutines\n]);\n\n$server->on(\'open\', function (Swoole\\WebSocket\\Server $server, $request) {\n    echo \"Client connected: {$request->fd}\\n\";\n});\n\n$server->on(\'message\', function (Swoole\\WebSocket\\Server $server, $frame) {\n    // Broadcast to all active connections:\n    foreach ($server->connections as $fd) {\n        if ($server->isEstablished($fd)) {\n            $server->push($fd, $frame->data);\n        }\n    }\n});\n\n$server->start();\n```', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2679, 'What is Laravel Reverb in Laravel 11, and how does it provide high-speed first-party WebSocket broadcasting?', '### Laravel Reverb Architecture\n\n**Laravel Reverb** is a first-party, high-performance WebSocket server built specifically for Laravel, designed with event-driven non-blocking I/O.\n\n```\n[Laravel App] ---> [Redis Pub/Sub] ---> [Laravel Reverb Server] ---> [Laravel Echo Clients]\n```\n\n#### Features & Performance:\n- **Pusher Protocol Compatible**: Drop-in replacement for Pusher or Soketi without modifying client-side JavaScript.\n- **Built-in Horizontal Scaling**: Natively scales across multiple server instances using Redis Pub/Sub.\n- **Zero External Dependencies**: Runs directly from PHP CLI via `php artisan reverb:start`.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2680, 'How do Public, Private, and Presence Channels work in Laravel WebSockets and how do you authorize client access?', '### Laravel Broadcast Channels & Authorization\n\n```\n+--------------------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| Channel Type       | Visibility                       | Authentication Required           |\n+--------------------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n| Public Channel     | Anyone can subscribe             | No                                |\n| Private Channel    | Authenticated users only         | Yes (Broadcast::channel)          |\n| Presence Channel   | Private + tracks user awareness  | Yes (Returns user profile data)   |\n+--------------------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\n```\n\n#### Channel Authorization Definition (`routes/channels.php`):\n```php\n// Private Channel (only order owner can listen):\nBroadcast::channel(\'orders.{orderId}\', function (User $user, int $orderId) {\n    return $user->id === Order::find($orderId)?->user_id;\n});\n\n// Presence Channel (returns user data for chat room):\nBroadcast::channel(\'chat.{roomId}\', function (User $user, int $roomId) {\n    if ($user->canJoinRoom($roomId)) {\n        return [\'id\' => $user->id, \'name\' => $user->name, \'avatar\' => $user->avatar_url];\n    }\n});\n```', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2681, 'How do you configure Nginx as a Reverse Proxy with SSL/TLS termination for a PHP WebSocket server?', '### Nginx Reverse Proxy for WebSockets\n\n```nginx\nmap $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {\n    default upgrade;\n    \'\'      close;\n}\n\nserver {\n    listen 443 ssl http2;\n    server_name ws.example.com;\n\n    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/privkey.pem;\n\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;\n        \n        # Increase timeouts for long-lived WebSocket connections:\n        proxy_read_timeout 86400s;\n        proxy_send_timeout 86400s;\n    }\n}\n```', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2682, 'How do you prevent memory leaks and manage long-running state in persistent PHP WebSocket servers?', '### Managing Memory in PHP Daemons\n\nIn standard PHP, memory is freed at the end of the HTTP request. In WebSocket daemons, memory leaks accumulate over days and crash the process.\n\n#### Best Practices:\n1. **Use `SplObjectStorage` or `WeakMap`**: Always detach client connections on disconnect to allow garbage collection.\n2. **Avoid Unbounded Static Arrays**: Do not push messages to global arrays without bounds checking or eviction.\n3. **Run Garbage Collection Periodically**: Trigger `gc_collect_cycles()` on idle intervals.\n4. **Database Reconnection**: Close or ping long-running PDO database connections to prevent `2006 MySQL server has gone away`.\n5. **Supervisor Auto-Restart**: Use Supervisor with memory limits (`memory_limit` / `max_requests`) to gracefully cycle workers.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2683, 'How does Workerman (`workerman/workerman`) implement multi-process WebSocket clustering in PHP?', '### Workerman Architecture\n\nWorkerman uses master-worker multi-process architecture with POSIX signals and event loops.\n\n```php\nuse Workerman\\Worker;\n\nrequire_once __DIR__ . \'/vendor/autoload.php\';\n\n$ws_worker = new Worker(\'websocket://0.0.0.0:2346\');\n$ws_worker->count = 4; // 4 concurrent worker processes (1 per CPU core)\n\n$ws_worker->onConnect = function ($connection) {\n    echo \"New connection\\n\";\n};\n\n$ws_worker->onMessage = function ($connection, $data) {\n    $connection->send(\'Hello \' . $data);\n};\n\nWorker::runAll();\n```', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2684, 'How do you scale PHP WebSockets horizontally across multiple servers using a Redis Pub/Sub message backplane?', '### Multi-Node WebSocket Scaling via Redis Pub/Sub\n\nWhen Client A is connected to Server 1 and Client B is connected to Server 2, broadcasting directly in local memory fails.\n\n```\n[Client A] ---> [Server 1 (PHP WS)] <--- Redis Pub/Sub Channel ---> [Server 2 (PHP WS)] <--- [Client B]\n```\n\n1. When Server 1 receives a message, it publishes the payload to a shared Redis channel (`PUBLISH chat_room message`).\n2. All PHP WebSocket server instances subscribe to Redis channels (`SUBSCRIBE chat_room`).\n3. Upon receiving the Redis event, each server fans out the frame to its locally connected WebSocket clients.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2685, 'How do you implement authentication for PHP WebSockets using JSON Web Tokens (JWT) vs Session Cookies?', '### WebSocket Authentication Strategies\n\nSince WebSockets cannot send custom HTTP headers during client-side JavaScript connection (`new WebSocket(...)`), use one of these two methods:\n\n1. **Query Parameter Token**: Pass JWT in connection URL (`ws://server/ws?token=eyJhbGciOi...`). The PHP server parses `$_GET[\'token\']`, validates the signature during the HTTP upgrade handshake, and rejects invalid connections (`401 Unauthorized`).\n2. **Ticket / Handshake Auth**: The client requests a single-use random ticket from a standard authenticated REST API, then connects to WebSockets with `?ticket=abc123`. The PHP WebSocket server verifies and invalidates the ticket in Redis.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2686, 'How do you calculate the Sec-WebSocket-Accept handshake header manually in pure PHP without external libraries?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConcatenate Sec-WebSocket-Key with 258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11, calculate sha1($str, true), and base64_encode() the binary hash.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2687, 'How do you parse and unmask incoming binary WebSocket frames using PHP pack() and unpack() functions?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nExtract first 2 header bytes, read 4-byte masking key, and loop through payload applying XOR bitwise operator ($data[$i] ^ $mask[$i % 4]).\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2688, 'What are the differences between Laravel WebSockets (BeyondCode), Soketi, and Laravel Reverb?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nBeyondCode is legacy PHP-based; Soketi is Node.js/uWebSockets; Laravel Reverb is first-party PHP with native Redis clustering and zero Node dependencies.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2689, 'How do you broadcast background queue job progress updates to a live frontend progress bar in Laravel?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nDispatch an event implementing ShouldBroadcastNow from inside the queued job handle() method to send progress percentages instantly.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2690, 'How does the ReactPHP Event Loop (React\\EventLoop\\Loop) multiplex asynchronous stream resources in PHP?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nUses stream_select, epoll, or libevent to wait for read/write socket readiness without blocking execution.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2691, 'How do you implement heartbeat Ping and Pong timers in Ratchet / Swoole to disconnect dead zombie clients?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConfigure timer to send periodic WebSocket Ping frames; track client lastPongTimestamp and close connections missing Pong replies.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2692, 'How to restrict allowed origins (CORS / AllowedOrigins) in PHP WebSocket servers to prevent Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking (CSWSH)?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nValidate the incoming Origin header during HTTP upgrade handshake and reject connections from unauthorized domains with 403 Forbidden.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2693, 'How does Amphp (amphp/websocket-server) leverage PHP 8.1 Fibers for cooperative multitasking in WebSockets?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nFibers allow writing sequential-looking synchronous code that pauses and resumes non-blockingly under the hood.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2694, 'How to handle binary file and image transfers over WebSockets in PHP without running out of RAM?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nStream binary data in 64KB chunks using continuation frames or save received binary chunks directly to temporary disk files.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2695, 'How do you implement presence channel user lists with join/leave notifications in pure PHP WebSockets?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nMaintain a Redis Set of active user IDs per room and broadcast user_joined and user_left events on connect/disconnect.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2696, 'How to optimize PHP WebSocket worker processes with systemd and Supervisor for 24/7 high availability?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nCreate a systemd unit file with Restart=always, LimitNOFILE=65536, and supervise worker processes automatically.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2697, 'What are the differences between ShouldBroadcast and ShouldBroadcastNow in Laravel event broadcasting?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nShouldBroadcast queues event publishing to background Redis queue; ShouldBroadcastNow publishes synchronously to WebSocket server immediately.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2698, 'How to test and mock WebSocket broadcasting events in PHPUnit without running a live WebSocket server?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nUse Event::fake([OrderShippedEvent::class]) and Event::assertDispatched() in Laravel test suites.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2699, 'How does Ratchet WampServer implement the WebSocket Application Messaging Protocol (WAMP v1) in PHP?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nProvides standardized Publish/Subscribe and Remote Procedure Call (RPC) abstractions over raw WebSockets.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2700, 'How to benchmark and load test a PHP WebSocket server with thousands of simulated clients using Artillery or k6?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nRun multi-threaded WebSocket load scripts measuring connection handshake latency, message round-trip time, and server CPU usage.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2701, 'How do you calculate the Sec-WebSocket-Accept handshake header manually in pure PHP without external libraries?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConcatenate Sec-WebSocket-Key with 258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11, calculate sha1($str, true), and base64_encode() the binary hash.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2702, 'How do you parse and unmask incoming binary WebSocket frames using PHP pack() and unpack() functions?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nExtract first 2 header bytes, read 4-byte masking key, and loop through payload applying XOR bitwise operator ($data[$i] ^ $mask[$i % 4]).\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
