(2716, 'How do you calculate the Sec-WebSocket-Accept handshake header manually in pure PHP without external libraries?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConcatenate Sec-WebSocket-Key with 258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11, calculate sha1($str, true), and base64_encode() the binary hash.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2717, 'How do you parse and unmask incoming binary WebSocket frames using PHP pack() and unpack() functions?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nExtract first 2 header bytes, read 4-byte masking key, and loop through payload applying XOR bitwise operator ($data[$i] ^ $mask[$i % 4]).\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2718, 'What are the differences between Laravel WebSockets (BeyondCode), Soketi, and Laravel Reverb?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nBeyondCode is legacy PHP-based; Soketi is Node.js/uWebSockets; Laravel Reverb is first-party PHP with native Redis clustering and zero Node dependencies.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2719, 'How do you broadcast background queue job progress updates to a live frontend progress bar in Laravel?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nDispatch an event implementing ShouldBroadcastNow from inside the queued job handle() method to send progress percentages instantly.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2720, 'How does the ReactPHP Event Loop (React\\EventLoop\\Loop) multiplex asynchronous stream resources in PHP?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nUses stream_select, epoll, or libevent to wait for read/write socket readiness without blocking execution.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2721, 'How do you implement heartbeat Ping and Pong timers in Ratchet / Swoole to disconnect dead zombie clients?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConfigure timer to send periodic WebSocket Ping frames; track client lastPongTimestamp and close connections missing Pong replies.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2722, 'How to restrict allowed origins (CORS / AllowedOrigins) in PHP WebSocket servers to prevent Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking (CSWSH)?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nValidate the incoming Origin header during HTTP upgrade handshake and reject connections from unauthorized domains with 403 Forbidden.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2723, 'How does Amphp (amphp/websocket-server) leverage PHP 8.1 Fibers for cooperative multitasking in WebSockets?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nFibers allow writing sequential-looking synchronous code that pauses and resumes non-blockingly under the hood.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2724, 'How to handle binary file and image transfers over WebSockets in PHP without running out of RAM?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nStream binary data in 64KB chunks using continuation frames or save received binary chunks directly to temporary disk files.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2725, 'How do you implement presence channel user lists with join/leave notifications in pure PHP WebSockets?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nMaintain a Redis Set of active user IDs per room and broadcast user_joined and user_left events on connect/disconnect.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2726, 'How to optimize PHP WebSocket worker processes with systemd and Supervisor for 24/7 high availability?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nCreate a systemd unit file with Restart=always, LimitNOFILE=65536, and supervise worker processes automatically.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2727, 'What are the differences between ShouldBroadcast and ShouldBroadcastNow in Laravel event broadcasting?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nShouldBroadcast queues event publishing to background Redis queue; ShouldBroadcastNow publishes synchronously to WebSocket server immediately.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2728, 'How to test and mock WebSocket broadcasting events in PHPUnit without running a live WebSocket server?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nUse Event::fake([OrderShippedEvent::class]) and Event::assertDispatched() in Laravel test suites.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2729, 'How does Ratchet WampServer implement the WebSocket Application Messaging Protocol (WAMP v1) in PHP?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nProvides standardized Publish/Subscribe and Remote Procedure Call (RPC) abstractions over raw WebSockets.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2730, 'How to benchmark and load test a PHP WebSocket server with thousands of simulated clients using Artillery or k6?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nRun multi-threaded WebSocket load scripts measuring connection handshake latency, message round-trip time, and server CPU usage.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
