(2776, 'How do you calculate the Sec-WebSocket-Accept handshake header manually in pure PHP without external libraries?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nConcatenate Sec-WebSocket-Key with 258EAFA5-E914-47DA-95CA-C5AB0DC85B11, calculate sha1($str, true), and base64_encode() the binary hash.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2777, 'How do you parse and unmask incoming binary WebSocket frames using PHP pack() and unpack() functions?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nExtract first 2 header bytes, read 4-byte masking key, and loop through payload applying XOR bitwise operator ($data[$i] ^ $mask[$i % 4]).\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2778, 'What are the differences between Laravel WebSockets (BeyondCode), Soketi, and Laravel Reverb?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nBeyondCode is legacy PHP-based; Soketi is Node.js/uWebSockets; Laravel Reverb is first-party PHP with native Redis clustering and zero Node dependencies.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2779, 'How do you broadcast background queue job progress updates to a live frontend progress bar in Laravel?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nDispatch an event implementing ShouldBroadcastNow from inside the queued job handle() method to send progress percentages instantly.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2780, 'How does the ReactPHP Event Loop (React\\EventLoop\\Loop) multiplex asynchronous stream resources in PHP?', '### WebSockets in PHP Engineering\n\nUses stream_select, epoll, or libevent to wait for read/write socket readiness without blocking execution.\n\n#### Real-Time PHP Architecture Rule:\nRun WebSocket servers as long-running CLI daemons (Swoole / Workerman / Reverb), manage memory meticulously, and scale horizontally using Redis Pub/Sub.', 'WebSockets in PHP from Zero to Advanced'),
(2781, 'How does Swoole Coroutine Hooking (`Runtime::enableCoroutine()`) convert blocking PDO and Redis calls into non-blocking async operations?', '### Swoole Coroutine Hooking\n\nIn standard PHP, calling `$pdo->query()` or `$redis->get()` blocks the entire operating system thread until the database responds.\n\n- **Coroutine Hooking**: Swoole replaces underlying Zend Engine C socket functions (`php_stream`, `socket`, `getaddrinfo`) with non-blocking coroutine equivalents.\n- When a coroutine executes a database query, Swoole automatically yields execution (**`coroutine_yield`**) to other ready coroutines on the same thread without blocking the WebSocket event loop.\n\n```php\nuse Swoole\\Runtime;\nuse function Swoole\\Coroutine\\run;\nuse function Swoole\\Coroutine\\go;\n\nRuntime::enableCoroutine(SWOOLE_HOOK_ALL);\n\nrun(function () {\n    go(function () {\n        // Non-blocking PDO execution in coroutine:\n        $pdo = new PDO(\'mysql:host=127.0.0.1;dbname=app\', \'root\', \'secret\');\n        $user = $pdo->query(\'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 1\')->fetch();\n    });\n});\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2782, 'How do Swoole Shared Memory Tables (`Swoole\\Table`) enable high-speed lock-free state sharing across multiple worker processes?', '### `Swoole\\Table` Shared Memory Architecture\n\nStandard PHP processes have isolated memory spaces. Sharing state usually requires slow external Redis queries.\n\n- **`Swoole\\Table`**: Allocates memory in shared RAM accessible by all worker processes using high-speed Row-Level Locking and CAS (Compare-And-Swap) atomic operations.\n\n```php\n$table = new Swoole\\Table(65536); // Allocates memory for 65,536 entries\n$table->column(\'fd\', Swoole\\Table::TYPE_INT);\n$table->column(\'user_id\', Swoole\\Table::TYPE_INT);\n$table->column(\'room_id\', Swoole\\Table::TYPE_STRING, 64);\n$table->column(\'last_active\', Swoole\\Table::TYPE_INT);\n$table->create();\n\n// Fast in-memory state lookup across all workers (sub-microsecond):\n$table->set($fd, [\'fd\' => $fd, \'user_id\' => 101, \'room_id\' => \'crypto_room\', \'last_active\' => time()]);\n$userData = $table->get($fd);\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2783, 'How do PHP 8.1+ Fibers work under the hood in modern asynchronous WebSocket servers like Revolt and Amp v3?', '### PHP 8.1+ Fibers Concurrency Mechanics\n\nA **Fiber** represents a full-stack, interruptible execution context (lightweight userland thread) managed entirely within the PHP runtime.\n\n```\n[Event Loop] ---> Fiber::start() ---> Running ---> Fiber::suspend() ---> Paused (Yields CPU)\n      ^                                                                      |\n      +------------------- (I/O Ready) ---> Fiber::resume() <----------------+\n```\n\n```php\n$fiber = new Fiber(function (): void {\n    echo \"Fiber started\\n\";\n    // Suspends fiber and yields control back to event loop:\n    $val = Fiber::suspend(\'waiting_for_socket\');\n    echo \"Fiber resumed with value: {$val}\\n\";\n});\n\n$status = $fiber->start(); // Output: Fiber started\n// Event loop handles other connections...\n$fiber->resume(\'socket_data_ready\'); // Output: Fiber resumed with value: socket_data_ready\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2784, 'How do you implement Graceful Zero-Downtime Hot Reloads in high-scale PHP WebSocket servers using POSIX signals?', '### Zero-Downtime Graceful Hot Reloads\n\nIn WebSocket servers, restarting the master process drops all active client connections. **Graceful Reload** reloads business logic without dropping TCP connections.\n\n```\n[CLI] --- SIGUSR1 ---> [Master Process] ---> Signals Manager Process\n                                                     |\n                         +---------------------------+---------------------------+\n                         | (Worker 1)                | (Worker 2)                |\n                         | Finish existing tasks     | Finish existing tasks     |\n                         | Terminate gracefully      | Terminate gracefully      |\n                         v                           v\n                     [Spawn New Worker with Updated PHP Code]\n```\n\n1. Send `kill -USR1 <master_pid>`.\n2. Master stops routing new events to old workers and spawns new worker processes containing the updated PHP files.\n3. Existing client TCP file descriptors remain established in the Master Reactor process without disconnection.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2785, 'How do you detect and diagnose circular reference memory leaks in long-running PHP WebSocket daemons?', '### Diagnosing Memory Leaks in PHP Daemons\n\n```php\n// ❌ Circular Reference Memory Leak in Event Listeners:\nclass Session {\n    public $onMessage;\n    public function __construct() {\n        // $this holds closure, closure captures $this by value -> Circular Cycle!\n        $this->onMessage = function($msg) { $this->handle($msg); };\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Diagnostic Solutions:\n1. **Use `WeakReference` and `WeakMap`**: Prevents closures from artificially incrementing reference counts.\n2. **`gc_status()` & `gc_collect_cycles()`**: Monitor cycle collector buffer.\n3. **Memory Snapshots**: Dump heap using `php-meminfo` or `memory_get_usage(true)` diffs between connection lifecycles.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2786, 'How do you implement custom Backpressure and Send Buffer flow control to handle slow WebSocket consumers in PHP?', '### Custom Backpressure Flow Control in PHP\n\n```php\n$server->on(\'message\', function (Swoole\\WebSocket\\Server $server, $frame) {\n    $clientInfo = $server->getClientInfo($frame->fd);\n    \n    // Check outbound socket buffer backlog:\n    if ($clientInfo[\'recv_queued_bytes\'] > 1024 * 1024 || $server->getSocket($frame->fd)->out_buffer_length > 1024 * 1024) {\n        // High-watermark exceeded (1MB backlog on slow client):\n        $server->pause($frame->fd); // Pause reading from slow socket\n        // Buffer critical messages in memory queue or drop ephemeral data\n    }\n});\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2787, 'How does binary message serialization with MessagePack (`ext-msgpack`) outperform JSON in high-frequency PHP WebSockets?', '### MessagePack Binary Serialization vs JSON\n\n```\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n| Metric                | JSON (json_encode)          | MessagePack (msgpack_pack)  |\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n| Payload Size          | Larger (Text ASCII keys)    | 40%–60% smaller (Binary IDs)|\n| Serialization CPU     | Higher (String escaping)    | Sub-microsecond (Binary)    |\n| Binary Data Support   | Requires Base64 (33% bloat) | Native raw byte buffer      |\n| PHP Extension         | ext-json                    | ext-msgpack                 |\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n```\n\n```php\n// Pack order book delta to binary:\n$binaryPayload = msgpack_pack([\n    \'type\' => \'depth_update\',\n    \'symbol\' => \'BTCUSDT\',\n    \'bids\' => [[65000.50, 1.45], [64990.00, 3.20]],\n    \'ts\' => microtime(true)\n]);\n$server->push($fd, $binaryPayload, SWOOLE_WEBSOCKET_OPCODE_BINARY);\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2788, 'How do you design a High-Scale Multi-Node WebSocket Fan-Out Cluster in PHP using Redis Cluster and Consistent Hashing?', '### Distributed Multi-Node PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\n```\n[Load Balancer (HAProxy / Nginx)]\n      |\n      +-----------------------+-----------------------+\n      | (Consistent Hash / IP)| (Consistent Hash / IP)\n      v                       v\n[Node 1 (PHP Swoole WS)]  [Node 2 (PHP Swoole WS)]  [Node N (PHP Swoole WS)]\n      |                       |                       |\n      +-----------------------+-----------------------+\n                              |\n                [Redis Cluster Pub/Sub Shards]\n```\n\n- HAProxy routes incoming clients based on IP / User ID hash to preserve server affinity.\n- Nodes publish updates to partitioned Redis Pub/Sub channels (`channel_{hash % 16384}`), eliminating broadcast storm bottlenecks across millions of clients.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2789, 'How do you optimize Linux kernel TCP parameters (`SO_REUSEPORT`, `tcp_max_syn_backlog`, `somaxconn`) for 100K+ concurrent PHP WebSockets?', '### Linux Kernel Tuning for 100K+ WebSockets\n\n```ini\n# /etc/sysctl.conf\n\n# Max open files per process:\nfs.file-max = 2097152\n\n# TCP connection backlog queues:\nnet.core.somaxconn = 65535\nnet.ipv4.tcp_max_syn_backlog = 65535\n\n# Ephemeral port range:\nnet.ipv4.ip_local_port_range = 1024 65535\n\n# TCP buffer memory allocation (min, default, max in bytes):\nnet.ipv4.tcp_rmem = 4096 87380 16777216\nnet.ipv4.tcp_wmem = 4096 65536 16777216\n\n# Enable TCP fast open and reuse:\nnet.ipv4.tcp_tw_reuse = 1\n```\nEnable `SO_REUSEPORT` in Swoole/Workerman so multiple worker processes bind the listening port directly, letting the Linux kernel load-balance incoming connections across workers with zero lock contention.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2790, 'How do you implement Multi-Tenant dynamic channel isolation and JWT token validation in high-throughput PHP WebSockets?', '### Multi-Tenant WebSocket Isolation\n\n```php\n$server->on(\'open\', function (Swoole\\WebSocket\\Server $server, Swoole\\Http\\Request $request) {\n    $token = $request->get[\'token\'] ?? null;\n    \n    try {\n        $payload = JWT::decode($token, new Key($secret, \'HS256\'));\n        $tenantId = $payload->tenant_id;\n        $userId = $payload->user_id;\n        \n        // Store tenant binding in Swoole Table:\n        global $clientTable;\n        $clientTable->set($request->fd, [\n            \'tenant_id\' => $tenantId,\n            \'user_id\' => $userId\n        ]);\n    } catch (Exception $e) {\n        // Reject invalid authentication immediately during handshake:\n        $server->disconnect($request->fd, 4001, \'Unauthorized\');\n    }\n});\n```', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2791, 'How do Swoole Coroutine Channels (Swoole\\Coroutine\\Channel) implement CSP concurrency in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nChannels allow coroutines to communicate and synchronize data via push() and pop() with zero locks.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2792, 'What are the performance differences between ext-uv (libuv), ext-ev, and stream_select in PHP async runtimes?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nlibuv and ext-ev use O(1) epoll/kqueue event demultiplexing, while stream_select has an O(N) array scan limit of 1024 sockets.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2793, 'How to configure permessage-deflate WebSocket compression in Swoole without exhausting server memory?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nEnable websocket_compression => true in server settings and set compression_level => 3 for optimal CPU/RAM balance.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2794, 'How does TCP_NODELAY eliminate packet batching latency in real-time PHP trading ticker feeds?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nDisables Nagle\'s algorithm, forcing the network stack to transmit packets immediately without waiting for 40ms ACK buffers.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2795, 'How to manage Unix Domain Socket (UDS) IPC between PHP master coordinator and worker daemons?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nBypasses network TCP stack to exchange binary payloads between local processes at memory bus speeds.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2796, 'How to trace and profile PHP WebSocket daemon performance bottlenecks using Blackfire and OpenTelemetry?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nInstrument async event callbacks to trace function execution times, memory allocations, and I/O wait spans.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2797, 'What is the difference between Swoole Process Pools (Swoole\\Process\\Pool) and standard worker processes?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nProcess Pools manage detached long-running worker clusters with automatic health monitoring and restart on crash.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2798, 'How do you implement client heartbeat Ping/Pong monitoring in Swoole using heartbeat_check_interval?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nConfigure heartbeat_check_interval => 30 and heartbeat_idle_time => 60 so Swoole automatically closes inactive sockets at C level.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2799, 'How to protect PHP WebSocket daemons against memory fragmentation using Jemalloc (USE_ZEND_ALLOC=0)?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nDisable Zend\'s internal memory allocator to let Jemalloc manage memory pages directly with active defragmentation.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2800, 'How to design a distributed Presence Channel tracking system with Redis Sorted Sets and TTL heartbeats in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nStore connected user IDs in Redis ZSets with current timestamp scores and purge expired users with ZREMRANGEBYSCORE.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2801, 'What are the security risks of WebSocket frame fragmentation starvation and how to mitigate in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nEnforce max frame accumulation sizes and disconnect connections exceeding frame assembly deadlines.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2802, 'How does Revolt (revolt/event-loop) provide a standard async event loop interface across ReactPHP and Amp?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nDefines a unified global event loop driver supporting timers, stream IO, signals, and Fiber suspension.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2803, 'How to handle Database connection pool timeouts during high-concurrency WebSocket broadcast surges in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nUse asynchronous coroutine connection pools with acquire timeouts and minimum/maximum pool size boundaries.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2804, 'How to safely manage SSL/TLS certificate hot-reloading in persistent PHP WebSocket daemons?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nReload certificate and private key files on SIGHUP without restarting worker processes or dropping client connections.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2805, 'How do you build a real-time collaborative document synchronization server using CRDTs or OT in PHP WebSockets?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nProcess operational transformation operations or Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs) over binary WebSocket channels.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
