(2885, 'How to manage Unix Domain Socket (UDS) IPC between PHP master coordinator and worker daemons?', '### Advanced PHP WebSocket Architecture\n\nBypasses network TCP stack to exchange binary payloads between local processes at memory bus speeds.\n\n#### High-Scale Architecture Rule:\nLeverage Swoole coroutines and `Swoole\\Table` shared memory, tune Linux kernel TCP buffers, and implement zero-downtime hot reloads.', 'Advanced PHP WebSocket Internals & Async Architecture'),
(2886, 'What are the fundamental differences between Schema-First and Code-First GraphQL schema design in PHP?', '### Schema-First vs Code-First in PHP\n\n```\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n| Feature               | Schema-First (e.g. Lighthouse)| Code-First (e.g. GraphQLite)|\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n| Definition Method     | .graphql SDL files          | PHP 8 Attributes / Classes  |\n| Source of Truth       | Schema Definition Language  | PHP Code Typehints & Models |\n| Team Collaboration    | Frontend & Backend align on SDL| Backend writes PHP code first|\n| Directives Support    | Heavy (@all, @rules, @guard)| Middleware / Attributes     |\n+-----------------------+-----------------------------+-----------------------------+\n```\n\n- **Schema-First (Lighthouse)**: Clean separation of interface contract from implementation using directives.\n- **Code-First (GraphQLite/API Platform)**: Generates schemas automatically from PHP 8 classes via `#[Query]`, `#[Mutation]`, and `#[Field]` attributes.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2887, 'How do you build a pure GraphQL server in PHP using `webonyx/graphql-php`?', '### webonyx/graphql-php Implementation\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\GraphQL;\nuse GraphQL\\Type\\Schema;\nuse GraphQL\\Type\\Definition\\Type;\nuse GraphQL\\Type\\Definition\\ObjectType;\n\n// 1. Define Type\n$userType = new ObjectType([\n    \'name\' => \'User\',\n    \'fields\' => [\n        \'id\' => [\'type\' => Type::nonNull(Type::int())],\n        \'name\' => [\'type\' => Type::string()],\n        \'email\' => [\'type\' => Type::string()],\n    ]\n]);\n\n// 2. Define Query Root\n$queryType = new ObjectType([\n    \'name\' => \'Query\',\n    \'fields\' => [\n        \'user\' => [\n            \'type\' => $userType,\n            \'args\' => [\'id\' => [\'type\' => Type::nonNull(Type::int())]],\n            \'resolve\' => fn($root, $args) => User::find($args[\'id\'])\n        ]\n    ]\n]);\n\n// 3. Execute Query\n$schema = new Schema([\'query\' => $queryType]);\n$rawInput = file_get_contents(\'php://input\');\n$input = json_decode($rawInput, true);\n\n$result = GraphQL::executeQuery($schema, $input[\'query\'], null, null, $input[\'variables\'] ?? null);\nheader(\'Content-Type: application/json\');\necho json_encode($result->toArray());\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2888, 'How does the DataLoader pattern solve the N+1 query problem in PHP GraphQL resolvers using Deferred promises?', '### The DataLoader Pattern & `GraphQL\\Deferred`\n\nIn GraphQL, if a query requests 50 authors and each author resolves books, standard resolvers execute **1 query for authors + 50 queries for books** (N+1 Problem).\n\n```\nResolvers (Enqueue IDs: [1, 2, ... 50]) ---> Deferred Execution ---> Single SQL Batch (WHERE author_id IN (...))\n```\n\n```php\n// In webonyx/graphql-php with Deferred Resolution:\n\'books\' => [\n    \'type\' => Type::listOf($bookType),\n    \'resolve\' => function ($author, $args, $context) {\n        // 1. Enqueue author ID into buffer:\n        BookDataLoader::add($author->id);\n        \n        // 2. Return Deferred promise resolved at the end of the query layer:\n        return new GraphQL\\Deferred(function () use ($author) {\n            BookDataLoader::loadBuffered(); // Executes single batch SELECT ... WHERE author_id IN (...)\n            return BookDataLoader::getForAuthor($author->id);\n        });\n    }\n]\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2889, 'How do Lighthouse Directives (`@all`, `@find`, `@belongsTo`, `@hasMany`, `@rules`) accelerate GraphQL API development in Laravel?', '### Laravel Lighthouse Directives\n\nLighthouse maps Eloquent models directly to GraphQL schemas with zero controller boilerplate.\n\n```graphql\n# schema.graphql\n\ntype Query {\n    users: [User!]! @all\n    user(id: ID! @eq): User @find\n    posts: [Post!]! @paginate(defaultCount: 10)\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n    createPost(input: CreatePostInput! @spread): Post @create @guard\n    deletePost(id: ID! @whereKey): Post @delete @guard\n}\n\ntype User {\n    id: ID!\n    name: String!\n    email: String!\n    posts: [Post!]! @hasMany\n}\n\ninput CreatePostInput {\n    title: String! @rules(apply: [\"required\", \"min:3\"])\n    content: String! @rules(apply: [\"required\"])\n}\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2890, 'How do you implement Query Complexity Analysis and Max Query Depth validation to prevent Denial of Service (DoS) attacks in PHP GraphQL?', '### Query Complexity & Depth Limiting\n\nA malicious client can craft deeply nested recursive queries (e.g. `user { posts { author { posts { author ... } } } }`) that crash the server.\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\Rules\\QueryDepth;\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\Rules\\QueryComplexity;\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\DocumentValidator;\n\n// 1. Max Query Depth (Max 7 nested levels):\nDocumentValidator::addRule(new QueryDepth(7));\n\n// 2. Max Query Complexity (Calculates weighted cost of requested fields):\nDocumentValidator::addRule(new QueryComplexity(100));\n\n// Custom field cost:\n\'heavyCalculation\' => [\n    \'type\' => Type::string(),\n    \'complexity\' => fn($childrenComplexity, $args) => $childrenComplexity + 20,\n];\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2891, 'How does Cursor-Based Pagination follow the Relay Connection Specification in PHP GraphQL?', '### Relay Cursor-Based Pagination\n\n```graphql\ntype Query {\n    users(first: Int, after: String): UserConnection!\n}\n\ntype UserConnection {\n    edges: [UserEdge!]!\n    pageInfo: PageInfo!\n}\n\ntype UserEdge {\n    node: User!\n    cursor: String!\n}\n\ntype PageInfo {\n    hasNextPage: Boolean!\n    hasPreviousPage: Boolean!\n    startCursor: String\n    endCursor: String\n}\n```\nIn Laravel Lighthouse: simply use `@paginate(type: CONNECTION)`.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2892, 'How do custom GraphQL Directives in PHP enforce field-level permissions, uppercase transformations, or sensitive data masking?', '### Custom GraphQL Directives in PHP\n\n```graphql\ndirective @hasPermission(role: String!) on FIELD_DEFINITION\n\ntype User {\n    id: ID!\n    name: String!\n    salary: Float! @hasPermission(role: \"HR_MANAGER\")\n}\n```\n\n```php\n// In custom Directive class:\npublic function handleField(FieldValue $fieldValue, Closure $next): FieldValue {\n    $role = $this->directiveArgValue(\'role\');\n    $resolver = $fieldValue->getResolver();\n\n    $fieldValue->setResolver(function ($root, array $args, GraphQLContext $context, ResolveInfo $info) use ($resolver, $role) {\n        if (!$context->user()?->hasRole($role)) {\n            return null; // Mask field or throw AuthorizationException\n        }\n        return $resolver($root, $args, $context, $info);\n    });\n\n    return $next($fieldValue);\n}\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2893, 'How do GraphQL Subscriptions in PHP push real-time updates over WebSockets using Laravel Echo and Redis?', '### GraphQL Subscriptions in PHP\n\n```graphql\ntype Subscription {\n    postCreated: Post! @subscription(class: \"App\\\\GraphQL\\\\Subscriptions\\\\PostCreated\")\n}\n```\n\n```php\n// In PostCreated Subscription class:\nclass PostCreated extends GraphQLSubscription {\n    public function authorize(Subscriber $subscriber, Request $request): bool {\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    public function filter(Subscriber $subscriber, $root): bool {\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\n// When post is created, broadcast subscription event to Redis/WebSockets:\n\\Nuwave\\Lighthouse\\Execution\\Utils\\Subscription::broadcast(\'postCreated\', $post);\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2894, 'How do you handle Multipart File Uploads in PHP GraphQL following the GraphQL multipart request specification?', '### File Uploads with GraphQL `Upload` Scalar\n\n```graphql\ntype Mutation {\n    uploadAvatar(file: Upload!): String!\n}\n```\n\n```php\n// Resolving Upload scalar in PHP:\n\'uploadAvatar\' => [\n    \'type\' => Type::string(),\n    \'args\' => [\'file\' => [\'type\' => \\GraphQL\\Type\\Definition\\Type::nonNull(\\Nuwave\\Lighthouse\\Schema\\Types\\Scalars\\Upload::class)]],\n    \'resolve\' => function ($root, array $args) {\n        /** @var \\Illuminate\\Http\\UploadedFile $file */\n        $file = $args[\'file\'];\n        $path = $file->store(\'avatars\', \'public\');\n        return $path;\n    }\n]\n```', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2895, 'Why and how should you disable GraphQL Introspection in production PHP environments?', '### Disabling Introspection for Security\n\nIntrospection allows attackers to discover all types, queries, mutations, and database structures.\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\Rules\\DisableIntrospection;\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\DocumentValidator;\n\n// In AppServiceProvider or production bootstrap:\nif (app()->isProduction()) {\n    DocumentValidator::addRule(new DisableIntrospection());\n}\n```\n*In Lighthouse `config/lighthouse.php`: set `\'security.disable_introspection\' => true`.*', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2896, 'How do Union Types and Interfaces differ in PHP GraphQL and how do you resolve types using __resolveType?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInterfaces define shared fields; Unions combine unrelated types; __resolveType returns the concrete ObjectType instance during execution.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2897, 'What are Input Object Types in GraphQL and why can they not be used as query return types?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInput objects carry structured arguments into mutations/queries; they cannot contain fields with arguments or circular output references.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2898, 'How do you implement Custom Scalar types (e.g. Email, DateTime, JSON) in webonyx/graphql-php?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nExtend ScalarType and implement serialize() (outbound), parseValue() (inbound variables), and parseLiteral() (inbound AST nodes).\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2899, 'How does Apollo Federation operate in PHP microservices using @key, @extends, and @external directives?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAllows composing multiple independent PHP GraphQL microservice schemas into a unified distributed supergraph gateway.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2900, 'How do you format and mask errors in PHP GraphQL using the ErrorFormatter and ClientAware interface?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nImplement ClientAware on custom domain exceptions to expose safe user messages while masking internal database errors in production.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2901, 'How does Field Selection AST parsing allow resolving only fields explicitly requested in the query?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInspect $resolveInfo->getFieldSelection() to include only requested columns in SQL SELECT queries, eliminating over-fetching.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2902, 'What is the difference between @defer and @stream incremental delivery directives in modern GraphQL?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\n@defer streams slow non-critical sub-queries in subsequent chunked HTTP responses; @stream streams items of a list as they become available.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2903, 'How do you implement Response Caching in PHP GraphQL using Redis and the @cache directive?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nCaches serialized query response payloads in Redis keyed by user ID and hashed query variables with automated tag-based invalidation.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2904, 'How to integrate Laravel Sanctum token authentication with GraphQL context and @guard directive?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nPass Sanctum bearer token in HTTP Authorization header; Lighthouse @guard directive verifies token and attaches User to GraphQL context.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2905, 'How does GraphQLite use PHP 8 Attributes (#[Query], #[Mutation], #[Field]) to build type-safe APIs?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nScans PHP 8 controller methods and entity classes to generate schema types directly from PHP return typehints with zero SDL files.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2906, 'How do you handle Global ID encoding and decoding for Relay-compliant nodes in PHP?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nBase64 encodes \'TypeName:id\' (e.g. base64_encode(\'User:42\')) to guarantee globally unique identifiers across all entity types.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2907, 'How does Batch Query Execution operate when a client sends an array of multiple GraphQL queries in a single HTTP request?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nPHP parses the array of query objects and executes each sequentially or concurrently, returning an array of execution results in one round-trip.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2908, 'How to test GraphQL queries and mutations in PHPUnit using test helpers (graphQL, postGraphQL)?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nUse $this->graphQL(\'query { users { id } }\')->assertJson([\'data\' => [\'users\' => []]]) to test schema outputs in automated CI pipelines.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2909, 'What is Persisted Queries (Automatic Persisted Queries - APQ) and how does it reduce HTTP bandwidth?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nClient sends SHA-256 hash of query instead of full query string; PHP looks up cached query string in Redis, reducing request size from 10KB to 64 bytes.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2910, 'How do you log and trace GraphQL query execution times using OpenTelemetry and Apollo Tracing in PHP?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAttach field execution middleware to measure resolver resolution durations and export tracing metadata to Datadog or Jaeger.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
