(2938, 'How to test GraphQL queries and mutations in PHPUnit using test helpers (graphQL, postGraphQL)?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nUse $this->graphQL(\'query { users { id } }\')->assertJson([\'data\' => [\'users\' => []]]) to test schema outputs in automated CI pipelines.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2939, 'What is Persisted Queries (Automatic Persisted Queries - APQ) and how does it reduce HTTP bandwidth?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nClient sends SHA-256 hash of query instead of full query string; PHP looks up cached query string in Redis, reducing request size from 10KB to 64 bytes.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2940, 'How do you log and trace GraphQL query execution times using OpenTelemetry and Apollo Tracing in PHP?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAttach field execution middleware to measure resolver resolution durations and export tracing metadata to Datadog or Jaeger.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2941, 'How do Union Types and Interfaces differ in PHP GraphQL and how do you resolve types using __resolveType?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInterfaces define shared fields; Unions combine unrelated types; __resolveType returns the concrete ObjectType instance during execution.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2942, 'What are Input Object Types in GraphQL and why can they not be used as query return types?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInput objects carry structured arguments into mutations/queries; they cannot contain fields with arguments or circular output references.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2943, 'How do you implement Custom Scalar types (e.g. Email, DateTime, JSON) in webonyx/graphql-php?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nExtend ScalarType and implement serialize() (outbound), parseValue() (inbound variables), and parseLiteral() (inbound AST nodes).\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `category`) VALUES
(2944, 'How does Apollo Federation operate in PHP microservices using @key, @extends, and @external directives?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAllows composing multiple independent PHP GraphQL microservice schemas into a unified distributed supergraph gateway.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2945, 'How do you format and mask errors in PHP GraphQL using the ErrorFormatter and ClientAware interface?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nImplement ClientAware on custom domain exceptions to expose safe user messages while masking internal database errors in production.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2946, 'How does Field Selection AST parsing allow resolving only fields explicitly requested in the query?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nInspect $resolveInfo->getFieldSelection() to include only requested columns in SQL SELECT queries, eliminating over-fetching.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2947, 'What is the difference between @defer and @stream incremental delivery directives in modern GraphQL?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\n@defer streams slow non-critical sub-queries in subsequent chunked HTTP responses; @stream streams items of a list as they become available.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2948, 'How do you implement Response Caching in PHP GraphQL using Redis and the @cache directive?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nCaches serialized query response payloads in Redis keyed by user ID and hashed query variables with automated tag-based invalidation.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2949, 'How to integrate Laravel Sanctum token authentication with GraphQL context and @guard directive?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nPass Sanctum bearer token in HTTP Authorization header; Lighthouse @guard directive verifies token and attaches User to GraphQL context.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2950, 'How does GraphQLite use PHP 8 Attributes (#[Query], #[Mutation], #[Field]) to build type-safe APIs?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nScans PHP 8 controller methods and entity classes to generate schema types directly from PHP return typehints with zero SDL files.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2951, 'How do you handle Global ID encoding and decoding for Relay-compliant nodes in PHP?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nBase64 encodes \'TypeName:id\' (e.g. base64_encode(\'User:42\')) to guarantee globally unique identifiers across all entity types.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2952, 'How does Batch Query Execution operate when a client sends an array of multiple GraphQL queries in a single HTTP request?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nPHP parses the array of query objects and executes each sequentially or concurrently, returning an array of execution results in one round-trip.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2953, 'How to test GraphQL queries and mutations in PHPUnit using test helpers (graphQL, postGraphQL)?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nUse $this->graphQL(\'query { users { id } }\')->assertJson([\'data\' => [\'users\' => []]]) to test schema outputs in automated CI pipelines.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2954, 'What is Persisted Queries (Automatic Persisted Queries - APQ) and how does it reduce HTTP bandwidth?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nClient sends SHA-256 hash of query instead of full query string; PHP looks up cached query string in Redis, reducing request size from 10KB to 64 bytes.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2955, 'How do you log and trace GraphQL query execution times using OpenTelemetry and Apollo Tracing in PHP?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAttach field execution middleware to measure resolver resolution durations and export tracing metadata to Datadog or Jaeger.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
