(2989, 'How does Apollo Federation operate in PHP microservices using @key, @extends, and @external directives?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nAllows composing multiple independent PHP GraphQL microservice schemas into a unified distributed supergraph gateway.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2990, 'How do you format and mask errors in PHP GraphQL using the ErrorFormatter and ClientAware interface?', '### PHP & GraphQL Architecture\n\nImplement ClientAware on custom domain exceptions to expose safe user messages while masking internal database errors in production.\n\n#### GraphQL Best Practice:\nEliminate N+1 queries with DataLoader/Deferred resolution, disable introspection in production, and enforce query depth/complexity limits.', 'PHP & GraphQL Architecture from Zero to Advanced'),
(2991, 'How do you implement an Apollo Federation v2 Subgraph in PHP and resolve entities using `__resolveReference`?', '### Apollo Federation v2 Subgraph in PHP\n\nIn a federated supergraph, each PHP microservice owns a subgraph entity declared with `@key`.\n\n```graphql\n# Users Subgraph Schema\ntype User @key(fields: \"id\") {\n    id: ID!\n    name: String!\n    email: String!\n}\n\n# Orders Subgraph extending User entity:\nextend type User @key(fields: \"id\") {\n    id: ID! @external\n    orders: [Order!]!\n}\n```\n\n#### Entity Reference Resolver in PHP:\n```php\n\'User\' => [\n    \'__resolveReference\' => function (array $reference, $context, $info) {\n        // $reference contains { \'__typename\': \'User\', \'id\': \'101\' }\n        return User::find($reference[\'id\']);\n    },\n    \'fields\' => [\n        \'orders\' => fn($user) => Order::where(\'user_id\', $user[\'id\'])->get(),\n    ]\n];\n```\nThe Apollo Router queries `_entities(representations: [...])` in batches, fanning out across PHP subgraphs with zero over-fetching.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2992, 'How do you defend against GraphQL Alias Bombing and Array Multiplication DoS attacks in PHP?', '### Alias Bombing & Array Amplification Defenses\n\n- **Alias Bombing**: An attacker requests the same heavy field 500 times using aliases (`a1: heavyField, a2: heavyField, ...`), bypassing standard query depth rules.\n- **Array Amplification**: Nesting 1-to-N relationships (`users(first: 100) { posts(first: 100) { comments(first: 100) } }`) requests $100 \\times 100 \\times 100 = 1,000,000$ database rows in a single query.\n\n#### Defense Implementation:\n1. **Calculated Field Multiplier Complexity**: Compute complexity as `fieldCost * (argument \'first\' or defaultCount)`.\n2. **Alias Count Limiter Rule**: Enforce a custom AST validator rejecting operations with >20 aliases per query node.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2993, 'How do you implement a Token Bucket Rate Limiter based on calculated GraphQL Query Complexity Points using Redis in PHP?', '### Cost-Based Token Bucket Rate Limiting\n\nInstead of counting HTTP requests (where a simple query costs the same as a 10,000-point recursive query), rate-limit by **Query Complexity Points**.\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\Validator\\Rules\\QueryComplexity;\n\n// 1. Calculate query complexity cost before execution:\n$complexityRule = new QueryComplexity(1000);\n$cost = $complexityRule->getQueryComplexity();\n\n// 2. Deduct cost from Redis Token Bucket (e.g. 5000 points / minute limit):\n$redisKey = \"rate_limit:user:{$userId}:points\";\n$currentPoints = Redis::eval($luaTokenBucketScript, 1, $redisKey, $cost, 5000, 60);\n\nif ($currentPoints < 0) {\n    throw new CustomGraphQLException(\'Rate limit exceeded. Query cost: \' . $cost . \' points exceeds remaining budget.\');\n}\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2994, 'How do you combine `GraphQL\\Deferred` with Swoole Coroutines or PHP 8.1 Fibers for concurrent multi-service batching?', '### Async Coroutine Batching with `GraphQL\\Deferred`\n\nTraditional PHP DataLoaders wait until all synchronous resolvers finish before executing the batch. With Swoole coroutines, sub-service HTTP and gRPC calls execute concurrently.\n\n```php\n\'user\' => [\n    \'type\' => $userType,\n    \'resolve\' => function ($post) {\n        return new GraphQL\\Deferred(function () use ($post) {\n            // Dispatches non-blocking async gRPC/HTTP call inside coroutine channel:\n            $channel = new Swoole\\Coroutine\\Channel(1);\n            go(function () use ($channel, $post) {\n                $user = UserGrpcClient::get($post->author_id);\n                $channel->push($user);\n            });\n            return $channel->pop();\n        });\n    }\n]\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2995, 'How do you parse and transform GraphQL queries at runtime using the AST Visitor pattern (`GraphQL\\Language\\Visitor`) in PHP?', '### Runtime AST Visitor Transformation\n\n`GraphQL\\Language\\Visitor` allows traversing and modifying query AST nodes before validation.\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\Language\\Parser;\nuse GraphQL\\Language\\Visitor;\nuse GraphQL\\Language\\AST\\NodeKind;\n\n$documentNode = Parser::parse($query);\n\n$modifiedAST = Visitor::visit($documentNode, [\n    NodeKind::FIELD => function ($node) {\n        // Automatically rewrite legacy field name \'username\' to \'email\':\n        if ($node->name->value === \'username\') {\n            $node->name->value = \'email\';\n            return $node;\n        }\n    }\n]);\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2996, 'How do you implement Field-Level Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) using PHP 8 Attributes in GraphQL resolvers?', '### Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC)\n\n```php\n#[Attribute(Attribute::TARGET_METHOD | Attribute::TARGET_PROPERTY)]\nclass RequirePermission {\n    public function __construct(public string $permission, public ?string $ownerField = null) {}\n}\n\nclass UserResolver {\n    #[RequirePermission(\'users.view_salary\', ownerField: \'id\')]\n    public function getSalary(User $user, $context): ?float {\n        // ABAC Logic: Allowed if admin OR user is viewing their own salary\n        if ($context->user()->hasPermission(\'users.view_salary\') || $context->user()->id === $user->id) {\n            return $user->salary;\n        }\n        return null; // Mask field without throwing fatal exception\n    }\n}\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2997, 'How does Automatic Persisted Queries (APQ) and Strict Operation Whitelisting eliminate execution parsing overhead and secure production APIs?', '### APQ & Strict Operation Whitelisting\n\n1. **APQ Workflow**:\n   - Client sends SHA-256 hash of query: `{ \"extensions\": { \"persistedQuery\": { \"sha256Hash\": \"a3f...\" } } }`.\n   - If hash is cached in Redis/APCu, PHP skips parsing and executes immediately.\n   - If hash is missing (`PersistedQueryNotFound`), client sends full query once to register.\n2. **Strict Operation Whitelisting (Safeql)**: In production, **reject all raw query strings completely**. Only pre-approved queries in the server hash registry are permitted, neutralizing 100% of injection and query complexity attacks.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2998, 'How do you propagate W3C Distributed Tracing headers (`traceparent`) across federated PHP GraphQL subgraphs?', '### Distributed Tracing in GraphQL Subgraphs\n\nWhen a root query spans 5 federated PHP subgraphs, end-to-end latency must be traced.\n\n```php\n// In GraphQL Context Middleware:\n$traceParent = $request->header(\'traceparent\'); // 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01\n\n// Create OpenTelemetry / Jaeger Span:\n$tracer = OpenTelemetry::getTracer();\n$span = $tracer->spanBuilder(\'graphql.resolve.User\')\n               ->setParent(TraceContext::extract($traceParent))\n               ->startSpan();\n\n// Resolve field...\n$span->end();\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(2999, 'How do you implement Schema Stitching and runtime Supergraph Gateway composition in pure PHP?', '### Schema Stitching in PHP\n\nCombines multiple independent remote GraphQL schemas into a single unified root schema.\n\n```php\n// Fetch remote schemas via Introspection (in build step / cache):\n$authSchema = RemoteSchema::create(\'https://auth.internal/graphql\');\n$billingSchema = RemoteSchema::create(\'https://billing.internal/graphql\');\n\n// Merge schemas with type linking:\n$mergedSchema = SchemaStitcher::merge([\n    $authSchema,\n    $billingSchema,\n], [\n    \'User.invoices\' => fn($user) => RemoteQuery::delegate($billingSchema, \'invoicesByCustomer\', [\'customerId\' => $user->id])\n]);\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3000, 'How do you optimize AST parsing memory allocation using APCu / Redis query document caching in PHP?', '### AST Parsing Document Cache\n\nParsing large GraphQL queries with hundreds of fields into PHP AST objects consumes CPU cycles on every request.\n\n```php\nuse GraphQL\\Language\\Parser;\n\nfunction getParsedAST(string $query): \\GraphQL\\Language\\AST\\DocumentNode {\n    $cacheKey = \'graphql_ast:\' . md5($query);\n    \n    // Check fast in-memory APCu cache:\n    if (apcu_exists($cacheKey)) {\n        return apcu_fetch($cacheKey);\n    }\n    \n    $ast = Parser::parse($query);\n    apcu_store($cacheKey, $ast, 3600); // Cache parsed AST structure\n    return $ast;\n}\n```', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3001, 'What are the @override and @inaccessible directives in Apollo Federation v2 and how do they manage zero-downtime field migrations?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nOverride moves field ownership between subgraphs; inaccessible hides internal fields from public supergraph schemas.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3002, 'How do you design a custom Error Masking strategy that conforms to RFC 7807 Problem Details in PHP GraphQL?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nIntercepts uncaught exceptions and structures responses with status, title, detail, and traceId while stripping database error stack traces.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3003, 'How does the @defer directive stream slow GraphQL fields in chunked HTTP multipart responses in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nYields initial fast query results and streams deferred sub-objects over HTTP chunked transfer as promises resolve.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3004, 'What are the differences between Hash Routing and Dynamic Subscriptions in distributed GraphQL clusters?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nHash routing directs subscriptions by room ID; dynamic subscriptions publish events across Redis Streams to all connected nodes.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3005, 'How to prevent Cyclic Fragment Expansion attacks in PHP GraphQL document validators?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nDocumentValidator::addRule(new KnownFragmentNames()) and NoFragmentCycles rule to detect recursive fragment loops.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3006, 'How do you implement custom GraphQL Directive Transformers on Mutation Input Objects in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nTransforms input fields (e.g. trimming strings, hashing passwords, sanitizing HTML) before passing data to resolvers.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3007, 'What is the difference between Schema Introspection Masking and Field-Level Visibility Policies in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nMasking hides whole types based on user role; visibility policies dynamically redact specific field values while keeping schema shape.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3008, 'How do you build a multi-region GraphQL caching layer with Redis Cluster and Cache-Control extensions?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nAttaches @cacheControl(maxAge: 300, scope: PUBLIC) and caches serialized JSON subtrees across edge Redis replicas.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3009, 'How does Entity Federation handle cross-subgraph data joins without distributed deadlocks in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nFederation Router constructs directed acyclic execution graphs (DAGs), ensuring dependency order across subgraphs.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3010, 'How to benchmark GraphQL resolver execution times and memory allocations using Xdebug profiling and Webgrind?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nGenerates cachegrind dumps to identify slow resolver iterations, database latency bottlenecks, and AST memory overhead.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3011, 'How do you implement global unique Node IDs across federated PHP subgraphs according to Global Object Identification spec?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nBase64 encodes composite identifiers (e.g. base64_encode(\'users_subgraph:User:101\')) for universal Relay refetching.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3012, 'What is GraphQL Query Cost Estimation and how does it assign dynamic complexity weights based on argument multipliers?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nMultiplies nested field complexity by the pagination limit argument (e.g. limit: 50 -> 50x multiplier) to calculate true query load.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3013, 'How to configure Apollo Studio / Hive schema check pipelines in CI/CD to prevent breaking schema changes in PHP subgraphs?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nRuns schema comparison against live production registry in GitHub Actions to block breaking field drops or type changes.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3014, 'How do you implement Real-Time Live Queries in PHP GraphQL without WebSockets using Server-Sent Events (SSE)?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nStreams text/event-stream responses over persistent HTTP connections whenever underlying database records mutate.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3015, 'How does Type Registry caching and lazy type loading reduce memory footprint in massive PHP schemas?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nLoads GraphQL type definitions on-demand only when referenced during query execution, rather than instantiating 1,000 types on bootstrap.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
