(3060, 'How does Type Registry caching and lazy type loading reduce memory footprint in massive PHP schemas?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nLoads GraphQL type definitions on-demand only when referenced during query execution, rather than instantiating 1,000 types on bootstrap.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3061, 'What are the @override and @inaccessible directives in Apollo Federation v2 and how do they manage zero-downtime field migrations?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nOverride moves field ownership between subgraphs; inaccessible hides internal fields from public supergraph schemas.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3062, 'How do you design a custom Error Masking strategy that conforms to RFC 7807 Problem Details in PHP GraphQL?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nIntercepts uncaught exceptions and structures responses with status, title, detail, and traceId while stripping database error stack traces.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3063, 'How does the @defer directive stream slow GraphQL fields in chunked HTTP multipart responses in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nYields initial fast query results and streams deferred sub-objects over HTTP chunked transfer as promises resolve.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3064, 'What are the differences between Hash Routing and Dynamic Subscriptions in distributed GraphQL clusters?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nHash routing directs subscriptions by room ID; dynamic subscriptions publish events across Redis Streams to all connected nodes.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3065, 'How to prevent Cyclic Fragment Expansion attacks in PHP GraphQL document validators?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nDocumentValidator::addRule(new KnownFragmentNames()) and NoFragmentCycles rule to detect recursive fragment loops.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3066, 'How do you implement custom GraphQL Directive Transformers on Mutation Input Objects in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nTransforms input fields (e.g. trimming strings, hashing passwords, sanitizing HTML) before passing data to resolvers.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3067, 'What is the difference between Schema Introspection Masking and Field-Level Visibility Policies in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nMasking hides whole types based on user role; visibility policies dynamically redact specific field values while keeping schema shape.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3068, 'How do you build a multi-region GraphQL caching layer with Redis Cluster and Cache-Control extensions?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nAttaches @cacheControl(maxAge: 300, scope: PUBLIC) and caches serialized JSON subtrees across edge Redis replicas.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3069, 'How does Entity Federation handle cross-subgraph data joins without distributed deadlocks in PHP?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nFederation Router constructs directed acyclic execution graphs (DAGs), ensuring dependency order across subgraphs.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3070, 'How to benchmark GraphQL resolver execution times and memory allocations using Xdebug profiling and Webgrind?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nGenerates cachegrind dumps to identify slow resolver iterations, database latency bottlenecks, and AST memory overhead.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3071, 'How do you implement global unique Node IDs across federated PHP subgraphs according to Global Object Identification spec?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nBase64 encodes composite identifiers (e.g. base64_encode(\'users_subgraph:User:101\')) for universal Relay refetching.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
(3072, 'What is GraphQL Query Cost Estimation and how does it assign dynamic complexity weights based on argument multipliers?', '### Advanced PHP GraphQL & Federation Architecture\n\nMultiplies nested field complexity by the pagination limit argument (e.g. limit: 50 -> 50x multiplier) to calculate true query load.\n\n#### Enterprise GraphQL Architecture Standard:\nAdopt Apollo Federation v2 subgraphs, enforce token bucket complexity rate-limiting, and use operation whitelisting in production.', 'Advanced PHP GraphQL Internals & Federation'),
