(3448, 'How does Testcontainers eliminate differences between production databases and test environments?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nSpawns ephemeral real Docker containers (PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka) directly from test setup code and destroys them after tests.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3449, 'What is Assertion Roulette test smell and how do descriptive assertion messages fix it?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nHaving multiple unexplained assertions in one test where failure doesn\'t indicate which specific condition broke.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3450, 'How do you test time-dependent logic in TDD using Clock abstractions (PSR-20 ClockInterface / Carbon::setTestNow)?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nInjects a mockable clock interface rather than calling time() or new DateTime() directly in production code.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3451, 'What is the difference between Branch Coverage, Condition Coverage, and Path Coverage in code analysis?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nBranch checks all if/else paths; Condition checks all boolean sub-expressions; Path checks all possible execution combinations.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3452, 'How do you test Domain Events and Event-Driven architecture in TDD without hitting real message brokers?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nMock or spy the event dispatcher to assert that specific DomainEvent instances were published with correct payload properties.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3453, 'What is the Mystery Guest test smell and how does inline test data builders resolve it?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nWhen a test relies on hidden external fixture files, making it impossible to understand the test without reading outside files.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3454, 'How does Database Transaction Rollback (RefreshDatabase) speed up database integration tests?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nWraps each test in a database transaction and rolls back on teardown, avoiding expensive table truncations or migrations.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3455, 'What are Parameterized / Data Provider tests and how do they eliminate test method duplication?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nExecutes the same test logic against a matrix of input datasets (@dataProvider in PHPUnit / test.each in Jest).\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3456, 'How do you test asynchronous Promises and EventEmitters in Jest / Vitest without timing race conditions?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nUse async/await with resolve/reject matchers and mock timers (jest.useFakeTimers) to advance time deterministically.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3457, 'What is Characterization Testing (Approval Testing) and how does it enable safe legacy code refactoring?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nCaptures existing legacy output snapshots (Golden Master) to ensure refactoring does not alter baseline behavior.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3458, 'How do you test private methods in TDD without violating encapsulation or using reflection hacks?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nNever test private methods directly; test them through the public API methods that invoke them.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3459, 'What is the Ice Cream Cone Anti-Pattern in automated software testing?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nHaving thousands of slow, brittle UI/E2E tests and very few fast unit tests, resulting in slow and flaky CI feedback.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3460, 'How do you implement Mock Service Worker (MSW) in TypeScript for network-level API mocking?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nIntercepts HTTP requests at network layer using Service Workers, providing realistic API mocking for unit and integration tests.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3461, 'What is the AAA (Arrange, Act, Assert) testing pattern and how does it compare to Given-When-Then?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nArrange sets up dependencies and state; Act executes the behavior under test; Assert verifies results and state transitions.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3462, 'What are Flaky Tests and how do you diagnose non-deterministic test failures in CI pipelines?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nTests that pass and fail intermittently due to race conditions, shared database state, or timezone/clock dependencies.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
(3463, 'How does Testcontainers eliminate differences between production databases and test environments?', '### Test-Driven Development (TDD) Mastery\n\nSpawns ephemeral real Docker containers (PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka) directly from test setup code and destroys them after tests.\n\n#### TDD Core Rule:\nWrite tests before code, verify behavior rather than implementation details, and use mutation testing to guarantee test rigor.', 'Test-Driven Development (TDD) from Zero to Advanced'),
