(3706, 'How does Multi-Query Attention (MQA) and Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) reduce KV Cache memory in LLMs?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nShares Key and Value projection heads across multiple Query heads, drastically reducing KV cache size and speeding up decoding.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3707, 'What is FlashAttention and how does tiling and kernel fusion eliminate GPU High-Bandwidth Memory (HBM) bottlenecks?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nComputes softmax attention in SRAM tiles without writing intermediate N x N attention matrices to slow GPU HBM.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3708, 'How does Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) align LLMs using PPO vs Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nPPO trains a separate reward model and value network; DPO derives closed-form loss directly over preference pairs without reward models.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3709, 'What is the Reparameterization Trick in Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) and why is it necessary for backpropagation?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nExpresses latent variable z = mu + sigma * epsilon (where epsilon ~ N(0,1)) so gradients can flow backward through the mean and variance.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3710, 'How does SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique) generate synthetic samples for imbalanced datasets?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nInterpolates feature space lines between existing minority samples and their k-nearest minority neighbors.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3711, 'What is Cross-Entropy Loss and why is it preferred over Mean Squared Error (MSE) for classification tasks?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nPenalizes confident wrong predictions exponentially via logarithmic loss, providing steep gradients for rapid convergence.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3712, 'What are the differences between Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) and Variational Autoencoders (VAEs)?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nGANs use adversarial min-max game (sharp photorealistic outputs); VAEs use probabilistic latent modeling (stable training, slightly blurrier).\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3713, 'How does Early Stopping with patience prevent overfitting during model training?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nMonitors validation loss after each epoch and halts training when loss fails to improve for N consecutive epochs, rolling back to best weights.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3714, 'What is the difference between Data Drift and Concept Drift in production Machine Learning systems?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nData drift is a shift in input feature distribution P(X); Concept drift is a shift in the conditional relationship P(Y|X).\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3715, 'How does Quantization (FP16, INT8, INT4, NF4) reduce memory footprint and latency in deep learning inference?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nQuantizes 32-bit floating point weights into 8-bit or 4-bit integers with minimal loss in model accuracy.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3716, 'What are Activation Functions (ReLU, LeakyReLU, GELU, Swish) and why are non-linearities required in neural networks?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nWithout non-linear activations, stacking 100 neural network layers mathematically collapses into a single linear matrix multiplication.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3717, 'How does the Support Vector Machine (SVM) maximize the geometric margin using Lagrange Multipliers and Slack variables?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nFinds optimal separating hyperplane with maximum distance to support vectors, handling non-separable data via soft-margin slack variables.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3718, 'What is the difference between Stratified K-Fold Cross Validation and TimeSeriesSplit?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nStratified K-Fold preserves class balance across folds; TimeSeriesSplit respects temporal order, never training on future data.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3719, 'How do Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) achieve translation invariance using shared weights and pooling layers?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nSlides spatial filter kernels across feature maps, detecting local visual features regardless of their exact pixel coordinates.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3720, 'What is Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) and why is it superior to absolute sinusoidal positional embeddings in LLMs?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nEncodes relative token positions by rotating query and key vectors in complex 2D subspaces, naturally generalizing to longer context lengths.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3721, 'What is the difference between Precision, Recall, F1-Score, and ROC-AUC in classification evaluation?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nPrecision measures true positive accuracy; Recall measures capture rate of positives; F1 harmonic mean; ROC-AUC measures discrimination threshold ranking.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3722, 'How does Batch Normalization differ from Layer Normalization and Group Normalization in deep neural networks?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nBatchNorm normalizes across batch dimension (dependent on batch size); LayerNorm normalizes across feature dimensions (essential for Transformers).\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3723, 'What are the mathematical differences between Expectation-Maximization (EM) and K-Means clustering?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nK-Means performs hard cluster assignment; EM computes soft probabilistic cluster memberships using Gaussian distributions.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
(3724, 'How does Principal Component Analysis (PCA) find orthogonal axes of maximum variance using SVD?', '### Machine Learning & Deep Learning Mastery\n\nComputes eigenvectors of covariance matrix or performs Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) on centered feature matrices.\n\n#### Core ML Principle:\nUnderstand mathematical optimization foundations, prevent data leakage during preprocessing, and select appropriate evaluation metrics for your target objective.', 'Machine Learning & Deep Learning from Zero to Advanced'),
